dbba453892e451d346e9884e2dd86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/2b3ae4bb10edbba453892e451d346e9884e2dd86"}],"sha":"8ab2b9aca82b8b6fb89c19a8c78ec7185553ca87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/8ab2b9aca82b8b6fb89c19a8c78ec7185553ca87"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/810357?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pateatlau","id":810357,"login":"pateatlau","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDM1Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/2b3ae4bb10edbba453892e451d346e9884e2dd86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-13T11:15:35Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Laldingliana Tlau Vantawl"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-13T11:15:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add CD deployment plans and rename frontend dev commands (#84)\n\n* docs: add CD deployment plans and rename frontend dev commands\n\n- Add CD-POC-RAILWAY-VERCEL.md: Low-cost POC deployment guide (~$20-40/mo)\n  - Railway for backend (11 services + 4 DBs)\n  - Vercel for frontend (5 MFEs)\n  - Step-by-step implementation checklist\n  - Environment variables reference\n  - Troubleshooting guide\n\n- Add CD-IMPLEMENTATION-CHECKLIST.md: AWS production deployment checklist\n  - Docker configuration (Phase 2)\n  - AWS infrastructure setup (Phase 3)\n  - Staging and production CD pipelines (Phases 4-5)\n  - Database migration automation (Phase 6)\n  - Monitoring and security hardening (Phases 7-8)\n\n- Rename frontend dev commands for consistency:\n  - dev:mf → dev:frontend (HTTP mode)\n  - dev:mf:https → dev:frontend:https (HTTPS mode)\n  - dev:mf:shell → dev:frontend:shell\n  - dev:mf:remotes → dev:frontend:remotes\n\n- Update CICD.md with deployment options table and references\n\n- Update README.md:\n  - Version 0.3.2 → 0.4.0\n  - Add Frontend/MFE Security Hardening section (Phases 1-7)\n  - Update commands to new naming convention\n  - Add CD deployment status and documentation links\n\n- Add manual-pentest.sh security testing script with fixes:\n  - EXIT trap for summary printing\n  - Guard flags for pass/fail logic\n  - Safe JSON encoding with jq\n  - Runtime JWT token generation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): preserve original exit status in cleanup trap\n\nThe cleanup_and_summary trap now properly captures the exit status\nthat triggered the trap (0) and preserves it through the cleanup\nprocess. This ensures that script failures are not masked by the\ntrap''s own exit code.\n\n- Capture trap_exit_status at the start of cleanup_and_summary\n- Use non-zero trap status or stored ORIGINAL_EXIT_STATUS\n- Only set exit to 1 for print_summary failure if original was 0\n- Preserve original non-zero exit status in all cases\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(cd): implement round 2 expert review recommendations\n\nImplemented all remaining recommendations from principal architect review:\n\n- Add MFE manifest-based remote resolution section (most important gap)\n- Add gateway contract validation note (OpenAPI schema validation)\n- Add --configuration=production flag to all Nx build commands\n- Strengthen database reset warning with visual emphasis\n- Add pre-demo warmup checklist (high value for demo reliability)\n- Add platform rule alignment table showing compliance status\n- Update quality score from 8.7 to 9.4 per round 2 review\n\nAll platform rules now have ✅ status including manifest-based\nremote resolution which was the only remaining gap.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(cd): add Phase 7 demo video recording guide\n\nAdded comprehensive video recording section for 5-minute stakeholder demo:\n\n- Recording tools comparison (Loom, OBS, QuickTime, etc.)\n- Pre-recording setup checklist (browser, screen, data)\n- Detailed 5-minute video structure with timing\n- Full script outline with talking points for each section\n- Features to highlight vs. features to avoid showing\n- Recording tips for first-time video creators\n- Backup plan if live demo fails\n- Final video checklist before sharing\n\nRecommended tool: Loom for ease of use and automatic hosting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(cd): apply final minor refinements for precision and clarity\n\nApplied 4 final polish items from architect review:\n\n1. Clarified MFE manifest hosting path - explicit note that manifest\n   is served at /mfe-manifest.json via Vercel static hosting\n\n2. Added cache-control rule for mfe-manifest.json - ensures instant\n   rollback capability by preventing stale manifest caching\n\n3. Added REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS and RETRY_ATTEMPTS to env reference table\n   for documentation consistency\n\n4. Softened ''No Sleep Delays'' claim to ''Minimal Sleep - Configured to\n   avoid sleep delays for demo workloads'' for technical accuracy\n\nItem 5 (Nx parallel builds) noted as future optimization - not required\nfor current POC deployment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review comments for CD docs and pentest script\n\nPR Comment 1 - manual-pentest.sh:\n- Add TESTS_STARTED flag to track when tests actually run\n- Modify cleanup_and_summary to only print summary when TESTS_STARTED=true\n- Prevents spurious summary output for --help or unknown options\n\nPR Comment 2 - CD-POC-RAILWAY-VERCEL.md:\n- Add safer database rollback workflow with pre-check steps\n- Include prisma migrate status/diff commands before reset\n- Add interactive reset option (without --force) as recommended\n- Add pre-reset checklist to verify POC environment and data loss acceptance\n\nPR Comment 3 - CD-POC-RAILWAY-VERCEL.md:\n- Change RABBITMQ_URL from ''<cloudamqp-url-or-empty>'' to ''<your-cloudamqp-url>''\n- Add note clarifying RABBITMQ_URL is required with Phase 2.3 cross-reference\n\nPR Comment 4 - CD-POC-RAILWAY-VERCEL.md:\n- Fix grammar: ''Logout from customer'' -> ''Log out from customer account''\n- Use correct verb form (two words) instead of noun form\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(cd): fix linting and formatting issues in deployment plan\n\nPR review fixes:\n\n1. Blockquote formatting: Remove blank line between Timeout/Retry Policy\n   and Contract Validation blockquotes to form contiguous block\n\n2. Hyphenation: Change ''Rate Limiting'' to ''Rate-Limiting'' in section\n   headers (compound adjective modifier)\n\n3. Spelling: Change ''netbanking'' to ''net banking'' for clarity\n\n4. Missing env var: Add RABBITMQ_URL to API Gateway environment\n   variables block (Phase 2.4) with cross-reference note\n\n5. Markdown lint MD040: Add language identifiers to all fenced code\n   blocks - ''text'' for ASCII diagrams and scripts, ''bash'' for env vars\n   and shell commands, ''json'' for JSON, ''typescript'' for TS code\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"