thub.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/080b6427144b041dedcb0676cef3d0085c18c96f"}],"sha":"8fa308f8ad15954e3d024589902c713225756825","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/8fa308f8ad15954e3d024589902c713225756825"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/810357?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pateatlau","id":810357,"login":"pateatlau","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDM1Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/080b6427144b041dedcb0676cef3d0085c18c96f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-12T23:17:17Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Laldingliana Tlau Vantawl"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-12T23:17:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(auth): complete Phase 7 - Session & Auth Hardening (#82)\n\n* feat(auth): migrate refresh tokens to HttpOnly cookies\n\nPhase 7, Task 7.1: Migrate tokens to HttpOnly cookies\n\nSecurity improvements:\n- Refresh tokens now stored in HttpOnly cookies (XSS protection)\n- Cookies configured with SameSite=Strict (CSRF protection)\n- Secure flag enabled in production (HTTPS only)\n- Access tokens remain in memory only (short-lived, 15 min)\n\nBackend changes:\n- Add cookie-parser middleware to auth-service\n- Create cookie utilities for secure token management\n- Update login/logout/refresh endpoints to use cookies\n- Support both cookie and body-based tokens for compatibility\n\nFrontend changes:\n- Add withCredentials: true to axios instance\n- Update interceptors to include credentials in fetch\n- CORS headers updated for cookie support\n\nFiles:\n- apps/auth-service/src/utils/cookies.ts (new)\n- apps/auth-service/src/utils/cookies.spec.ts (new)\n- apps/auth-service/src/controllers/auth.controller.ts\n- apps/auth-service/src/main.ts\n- libs/shared-api-client/src/lib/apiClient.ts\n- libs/shared-api-client/src/lib/interceptors.ts\n- apps/api-gateway/src/middleware/cors.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): set HttpOnly cookie for OAuth login and fix Secure flag\n\n- OAuth callback now sets refresh token as HttpOnly cookie (was only in URL)\n- Fixed Secure cookie flag to be true for HTTPS in development (via nginx)\n- Updated oauth.controller.spec.ts to mock res.cookie\n\nThis fixes two issues:\n1. OAuth logins without MFA were not getting the HttpOnly cookie\n2. Cookies were not being set properly over HTTPS in development\n\nPOC-3 Phase 7.1: Session & Auth Hardening\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update Task 7.1 documentation with OAuth cookie support\n\n- Added OAuth controller to implementation details\n- Updated Secure flag note (true for both prod and dev)\n- Added oauth.controller.spec.ts to modified files list\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): remove token storage from localStorage (Task 7.2)\n\nSecurity hardening: Tokens no longer stored in localStorage to prevent\nXSS token theft. This completes Task 7.2 of Phase 7 - Session & Auth\nHardening.\n\nChanges:\n- Auth store: Remove refreshToken from state entirely (now in HttpOnly\n  cookie only)\n- Auth store: Access token kept in memory only (not persisted)\n- Auth store: Only user info and isAuthenticated persisted to\n  localStorage\n- Session sync: TOKEN_REFRESH event no longer includes token (security)\n- Session sync: Other tabs refresh via cookie on next API call\n- Event bus: auth:login and auth:token-refreshed no longer emit tokens\n\nToken flow after changes:\n- Access tokens: Memory only (Zustand state, cleared on page reload)\n- Refresh tokens: HttpOnly cookie only (set by server, not in JS)\n- User info: localStorage (non-sensitive, for immediate UI on reload)\n\nOn page reload, first API call triggers automatic token refresh via\nHttpOnly cookie, seamlessly restoring the session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): implement session fingerprinting (Task 7.3)\n\nPOC-3 Phase 7.3: Add client-side session fingerprinting to detect\nsession hijacking attempts.\n\nClient-side:\n- Generate fingerprint from browser characteristics (user-agent,\n  screen resolution, timezone, language, platform, hardware\n  concurrency, device memory, touch support, WebGL renderer)\n- SHA-256 hash of fingerprint data for compact transmission\n- Cache in memory and sessionStorage for performance\n- Add X-Client-Fingerprint header to all API requests\n- clearCachedFingerprint() on logout\n\nServer-side:\n- Combine server-side (IP, UA) and client fingerprint for enhanced\n  detection\n- Validate fingerprint on token refresh\n- Revoke session on fingerprint mismatch\n- Security logging with mismatch type detection\n\nFiles created:\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/session-fingerprint.ts\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/session-fingerprint.spec.ts\n\nFiles modified:\n- apps/auth-service/src/controllers/auth.controller.ts\n- apps/auth-service/src/services/auth.service.ts\n- apps/auth-service/src/services/token-blacklist.service.ts\n- libs/shared-api-client/src/lib/interceptors.ts\n- libs/shared-api-client/src/index.ts\n- libs/shared-utils/src/index.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): add session activity monitoring (Task 7.4)\n\nPOC-3 Phase 7.4: Comprehensive session activity monitoring to detect\nidle sessions, warn users before timeout, and provide session extension.\n\nCore features:\n- SessionActivityMonitor class tracks user activity (DOM events)\n- Configurable idle timeout (default 15 min, via NX_SESSION_TIMEOUT_MS)\n- Warning 2 minutes before session expires\n- Activity throttling (30s) to reduce storage writes\n- Cross-tab synchronization via BroadcastChannel\n- Persists last activity to localStorage for consistency\n\nReact integration:\n- useSessionActivity hook with state, extend(), start(), stop()\n- SessionTimeoutWarning modal with countdown timer\n- SessionActivityProvider wraps app in bootstrap.tsx\n- Auto-starts on authentication, stops on logout\n\nSession timeout presets:\n- strict: 5 min, standard: 15 min, relaxed: 30 min, extended: 60 min\n\nEvent bus updates (POC-3 7.2/7.4):\n- AuthLoginPayload: tokens removed for security\n- AuthTokenRefreshedPayload: token removed for security\n- AuthSessionExpiredPayload: added reason field\n\nFiles created:\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/session-activity.ts\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/session-activity.spec.ts\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/hooks/useSessionActivity.ts\n- apps/shell/src/components/SessionTimeoutWarning.tsx\n- apps/shell/src/components/SessionActivityProvider.tsx\n\nFiles modified:\n- apps/shell/src/bootstrap.tsx\n- libs/shared-utils/src/index.ts\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/hooks/index.ts\n- libs/shared-event-bus/src/lib/events/auth.ts\n- libs/shared-event-bus/src/lib/schemas.ts\n- libs/shared-event-bus/src/lib/schemas.spec.ts\n- libs/shared-auth-store/src/lib/shared-auth-store.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): complete session security testing (Task 7.5)\n\nPOC-3 Phase 7.5: Test Session Security - Final Phase 7 Task\n\nTest Implementation:\n- Created comprehensive session-security.spec.ts with 21 tests covering:\n  - Task 7.1: HttpOnly Cookie Configuration\n  - Task 7.2: Token Storage Security\n  - Task 7.3: Session Fingerprinting\n  - Task 7.4: Session Activity Monitoring\n  - API Client Configuration\n  - Cross-Tab Session Sync\n  - Session Expiration Events\n\nAPI Updates (POC-3 Phase 7.2 compliance):\n- Updated TokenProvider interface: setTokens → setAccessToken (single param)\n- Refresh token now exclusively in HttpOnly cookie (not in JS memory)\n- Updated all MFE API clients to use new token provider interface:\n  - payments-mfe/src/api/payments.ts\n  - admin-mfe/src/api/dashboard.ts\n  - admin-mfe/src/api/adminApiClient.ts\n  - profile-mfe/src/api/profile.ts\n  - profile-mfe/src/api/oauth.ts\n  - profile-mfe/src/api/mfa.ts\n- Updated interceptors.ts for cookie-based token refresh\n- Fixed OAuthCallback to use single-param setAccessToken\n\nTest Results:\n- shared-utils: 344 tests passing (including new session-security tests)\n- shared-api-client: 31 tests passing\n- shared-auth-store: 37 tests passing\n- All 32 projects build successfully\n\nPhase 7 Status: 100% Complete (5/5 tasks)\nOverall MFE Hardening: 100% Complete (42/42 tasks)\n\nSecurity features implemented:\n- HttpOnly cookies for refresh tokens (XSS protection)\n- Token storage removed from localStorage\n- Session fingerprinting (hijacking detection)\n- Session activity monitoring (idle timeout)\n- Cross-tab session synchronization\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(shared-utils): prefix unused variable with underscore\n\nFix lint error for unused variable ''initialActivity'' in throttle test\nby prefixing with underscore to indicate intentional non-use.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth-service): replace explicit any with proper Response type\n\nFix lint errors in cookies.spec.ts by using proper TypeScript types\ninstead of `as any` casts for mock response objects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(security): add comprehensive security testing infrastructure\n\nAdd security testing tools for Phase 7 Session & Auth Hardening:\n\n- scripts/security/security-test.sh: Comprehensive security testing script\n  - Cookie security verification (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite)\n  - Session fingerprinting tests\n  - Token storage verification\n  - CSRF protection tests\n  - Rate limiting tests\n  - Security headers audit\n  - OWASP ZAP integration\n\n- scripts/security/zap-rules.tsv: ZAP rule configuration for MFE app\n  - FAIL rules for critical security issues\n  - WARN rules for important issues\n  - IGNORE rules for dev-specific false positives\n\n- .github/workflows/security-scan.yml: Automated security scanning\n  - Manual trigger with scan type selection\n  - Weekly scheduled scans (Sundays at 2 AM UTC)\n  - ZAP baseline and API scans\n  - Security report artifacts\n  - Auto-create issue on failure\n\nNew npm scripts:\n  - pnpm security:test         - Run full security test suite\n  - pnpm security:test:quick   - Quick tests only (no ZAP)\n  - pnpm security:test:full    - Full tests including ZAP scan\n  - pnpm security:zap          - ZAP scan only\n  - pnpm security:zap:baseline - Docker ZAP baseline scan\n  - pnpm security:zap:api      - Docker ZAP API scan\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review comments for Phase 7 session hardening\n\nThis commit addresses all 19 PR review comments:\n\nCORS & API Gateway:\n- Add X-Client-Fingerprint to CORS allowedHeaders (#1)\n\nOAuth Controller:\n- Add TODO for removing refreshToken from URL after MFE migration (#2)\n\nAuth Service Security:\n- Mask email with maskEmailForLog in fingerprint mismatch log (#3)\n- Remove IP from token blacklist details to protect PII (#4)\n- Update cookie JSDoc to reflect path: ''/'' (#6)\n\nCookie Tests:\n- Fix maxAge test to handle env var variations (#5)\n\nSession Activity Provider:\n- Use refs for dev logging to avoid interval recreation (#7)\n\nSession Timeout Warning:\n- Replace manual focus trap with useFocusTrap hook (#8)\n\nAPI Client Interceptors:\n- Make fingerprint header async with ensureFingerprintHeader (#9)\n\nuseSessionActivity Hook:\n- Store callbacks in refs to avoid effect recreation (#10, #16)\n- Add eslint-disable comment explaining config exclusion\n\nSession Activity Monitor:\n- Fix formatTimeRemaining to use singular \"1 second\" (#11)\n- Handle structural config changes with restart in updateConfig (#12, #19)\n- Fix timeout broadcast storm with timeoutFromRemote flag (#13)\n- Fix unused variable in throttle test (#18)\n\nSession Fingerprint:\n- Fix timezone offset to use proper HH:MM format (e.g., UTC+05:30) (#14)\n- Fix msMaxTouchPoints non-null assertion with nullish coalescing (#15)\n- Remove unused timezone initial value (#17)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review comments for Phase 7 session hardening\n\n- Add try/catch to handleTimeout in SessionActivityProvider to prevent\n  unhandled promise rejections from async logout\n- Fix aria-live announcements in SessionTimeoutWarning: use aria-live=\"off\"\n  on timer display and add separate sr-only span that announces only\n  every 30 seconds or in last 10 seconds to avoid verbosity\n- Don''t cache empty fingerprints in interceptors to allow retry on\n  subsequent requests if initial fingerprint generation fails\n- Fix set -e arithmetic issue in security-test.sh by using $((PASSED + 1))\n  instead of ((PASSED++)) which is incompatible with errexit\n- Use FINGERPRINT variable in security test instead of hardcoded value\n- Fix PORT assignment in security-scan.yml with case statement\n- Update ZAP action versions to v0.15.0 and v0.10.0\n- Add label existence checking before issue creation in security workflow\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address additional PR review comments for security testing\n\n- Re-throw non-404 errors in security-scan.yml label checking loop\n  to fail fast on network/permission issues instead of silently ignoring\n- Change default BASE_URL and API_URL to HTTP in security-test.sh\n  for compatibility with local/CI runs that serve over plain HTTP\n- Remove unused RUN_QUICK variable from security-test.sh main()\n  as quick tests always run (only ZAP is conditional on --full flag)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"02dd597ce1d15c7faa3bad324b3c080d9212b285","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/git/trees/02dd597ce1d15c7faa3bad324b3c080d9212b285"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/git/commits/080b6427144b041dedcb0676cef3d0085c18c96f","verification":{"payload":"tree 02dd597ce1d15c7faa3bad324b3c080d9212b285\nparent 8bb85b0647efdeaefd854cd6efe65dec0da2ab4e\nauthor Laldingliana Tlau Vantawl <pateatlau@gmail.com> 1770938237 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770938237 +0530\n\nfeat(auth): complete Phase 7 - Session & Auth Hardening (#82)\n\n* feat(auth): migrate refresh tokens to HttpOnly cookies\n\nPhase 7, Task 7.1: Migrate tokens to HttpOnly cookies\n\nSecurity improvements:\n- Refresh tokens now stored in HttpOnly cookies (XSS protection)\n- Cookies configured with SameSite=Strict (CSRF protection)\n- Secure flag enabled in production (HTTPS only)\n- Access tokens remain in memory only (short-lived, 15 min)\n\nBackend changes:\n- Add cookie-parser middleware to auth-service\n- Create cookie utilities for secure token management\n- Update login/logout/refresh endpoints to use cookies\n- Support both cookie and body-based tokens for compatibility\n\nFrontend changes:\n- Add withCredentials: true to axios instance\n- Update interceptors to include credentials in fetch\n- CORS headers updated for cookie support\n\nFiles:\n- apps/auth-service/src/utils/cookies.ts (new)\n- apps/auth-service/src/utils/cookies.spec.ts (new)\n- apps/auth-service/src/controllers/auth.controller.ts\n- apps/auth-service/src/main.ts\n- libs/shared-api-client/src/lib/apiClient.ts\n- libs/shared-api-client/src/lib/interceptors.ts\n- apps/api-gateway/src/middleware/cors.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): set HttpOnly cookie for OAuth login and fix Secure flag\n\n- OAuth callback now sets refresh token as HttpOnly cookie (was only in URL)\n- Fixed Secure cookie flag to be true for HTTPS in development (via nginx)\n- Updated oauth.controller.spec.ts to mock res.cookie\n\nThis fixes two issues:\n1. OAuth logins without MFA were not getting the HttpOnly cookie\n2. Cookies were not being set properly over HTTPS in development\n\nPOC-3 Phase 7.1: Session & Auth Hardening\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update Task 7.1 documentation with OAuth cookie support\n\n- Added OAuth controller to implementation details\n- Updated Secure flag note (true for both prod and dev)\n- Added oauth.controller.spec.ts to modified files list\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): remove token storage from localStorage (Task 7.2)\n\nSecurity hardening: Tokens no longer stored in localStorage to prevent\nXSS token theft. This completes Task 7.2 of Phase 7 - Session & Auth\nHardening.\n\nChanges:\n- Auth store: Remove refreshToken from state entirely (now in HttpOnly\n  cookie only)\n- Auth store: Access token kept in memory only (not persisted)\n- Auth store: Only user info and isAuthenticated persisted to\n  localStorage\n- Session sync: TOKEN_REFRESH event no longer includes token (security)\n- Session sync: Other tabs refresh via cookie on next API call\n- Event bus: auth:login and auth:token-refreshed no longer emit tokens\n\nToken flow after changes:\n- Access tokens: Memory only (Zustand state, cleared on page reload)\n- Refresh tokens: HttpOnly cookie only (set by server, not in JS)\n- User info: localStorage (non-sensitive, for immediate UI on reload)\n\nOn page reload, first API call triggers automatic token refresh via\nHttpOnly cookie, seamlessly restoring the session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): implement session fingerprinting (Task 7.3)\n\nPOC-3 Phase 7.3: Add client-side session fingerprinting to detect\nsession hijacking attempts.\n\nClient-side:\n- Generate fingerprint from browser characteristics (user-agent,\n  screen resolution, timezone, language, platform, hardware\n  concurrency, device memory, touch support, WebGL renderer)\n- SHA-256 hash of fingerprint data for compact transmission\n- Cache in memory and sessionStorage for performance\n- Add X-Client-Fingerprint header to all API requests\n- clearCachedFingerprint() on logout\n\nServer-side:\n- Combine server-side (IP, UA) and client fingerprint for enhanced\n  detection\n- Validate fingerprint on token refresh\n- Revoke session on fingerprint mismatch\n- Security logging with mismatch type detection\n\nFiles created:\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/session-fingerprint.ts\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/session-fingerprint.spec.ts\n\nFiles modified:\n- apps/auth-service/src/controllers/auth.controller.ts\n- apps/auth-service/src/services/auth.service.ts\n- apps/auth-service/src/services/token-blacklist.service.ts\n- libs/shared-api-client/src/lib/interceptors.ts\n- libs/shared-api-client/src/index.ts\n- libs/shared-utils/src/index.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): add session activity monitoring (Task 7.4)\n\nPOC-3 Phase 7.4: Comprehensive session activity monitoring to detect\nidle sessions, warn users before timeout, and provide session extension.\n\nCore features:\n- SessionActivityMonitor class tracks user activity (DOM events)\n- Configurable idle timeout (default 15 min, via NX_SESSION_TIMEOUT_MS)\n- Warning 2 minutes before session expires\n- Activity throttling (30s) to reduce storage writes\n- Cross-tab synchronization via BroadcastChannel\n- Persists last activity to localStorage for consistency\n\nReact integration:\n- useSessionActivity hook with state, extend(), start(), stop()\n- SessionTimeoutWarning modal with countdown timer\n- SessionActivityProvider wraps app in bootstrap.tsx\n- Auto-starts on authentication, stops on logout\n\nSession timeout presets:\n- strict: 5 min, standard: 15 min, relaxed: 30 min, extended: 60 min\n\nEvent bus updates (POC-3 7.2/7.4):\n- AuthLoginPayload: tokens removed for security\n- AuthTokenRefreshedPayload: token removed for security\n- AuthSessionExpiredPayload: added reason field\n\nFiles created:\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/session-activity.ts\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/session-activity.spec.ts\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/hooks/useSessionActivity.ts\n- apps/shell/src/components/SessionTimeoutWarning.tsx\n- apps/shell/src/components/SessionActivityProvider.tsx\n\nFiles modified:\n- apps/shell/src/bootstrap.tsx\n- libs/shared-utils/src/index.ts\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/hooks/index.ts\n- libs/shared-event-bus/src/lib/events/auth.ts\n- libs/shared-event-bus/src/lib/schemas.ts\n- libs/shared-event-bus/src/lib/schemas.spec.ts\n- libs/shared-auth-store/src/lib/shared-auth-store.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): complete session security testing (Task 7.5)\n\nPOC-3 Phase 7.5: Test Session Security - Final Phase 7 Task\n\nTest Implementation:\n- Created comprehensive session-security.spec.ts with 21 tests covering:\n  - Task 7.1: HttpOnly Cookie Configuration\n  - Task 7.2: Token Storage Security\n  - Task 7.3: Session Fingerprinting\n  - Task 7.4: Session Activity Monitoring\n  - API Client Configuration\n  - Cross-Tab Session Sync\n  - Session Expiration Events\n\nAPI Updates (POC-3 Phase 7.2 compliance):\n- Updated TokenProvider interface: setTokens → setAccessToken (single param)\n- Refresh token now exclusively in HttpOnly cookie (not in JS memory)\n- Updated all MFE API clients to use new token provider interface:\n  - payments-mfe/src/api/payments.ts\n  - admin-mfe/src/api/dashboard.ts\n  - admin-mfe/src/api/adminApiClient.ts\n  - profile-mfe/src/api/profile.ts\n  - profile-mfe/src/api/oauth.ts\n  - profile-mfe/src/api/mfa.ts\n- Updated interceptors.ts for cookie-based token refresh\n- Fixed OAuthCallback to use single-param setAccessToken\n\nTest Results:\n- shared-utils: 344 tests passing (including new session-security tests)\n- shared-api-client: 31 tests passing\n- shared-auth-store: 37 tests passing\n- All 32 projects build successfully\n\nPhase 7 Status: 100% Complete (5/5 tasks)\nOverall MFE Hardening: 100% Complete (42/42 tasks)\n\nSecurity features implemented:\n- HttpOnly cookies for refresh tokens (XSS protection)\n- Token storage removed from localStorage\n- Session fingerprinting (hijacking detection)\n- Session activity monitoring (idle timeout)\n- Cross-tab session synchronization\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(shared-utils): prefix unused variable with underscore\n\nFix lint error for unused variable ''initialActivity'' in throttle test\nby prefixing with underscore to indicate intentional non-use.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth-service): replace explicit any with proper Response type\n\nFix lint errors in cookies.spec.ts by using proper TypeScript types\ninstead of `as any` casts for mock response objects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(security): add comprehensive security testing infrastructure\n\nAdd security testing tools for Phase 7 Session & Auth Hardening:\n\n- scripts/security/security-test.sh: Comprehensive security testing script\n  - Cookie security verification (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite)\n  - Session fingerprinting tests\n  - Token storage verification\n  - CSRF protection tests\n  - Rate limiting tests\n  - Security headers audit\n  - OWASP ZAP integration\n\n- scripts/security/zap-rules.tsv: ZAP rule configuration for MFE app\n  - FAIL rules for critical security issues\n  - WARN rules for important issues\n  - IGNORE rules for dev-specific false positives\n\n- .github/workflows/security-scan.yml: Automated security scanning\n  - Manual trigger with scan type selection\n  - Weekly scheduled scans (Sundays at 2 AM UTC)\n  - ZAP baseline and API scans\n  - Security report artifacts\n  - Auto-create issue on failure\n\nNew npm scripts:\n  - pnpm security:test         - Run full security test suite\n  - pnpm security:test:quick   - Quick tests only (no ZAP)\n  - pnpm security:test:full    - Full tests including ZAP scan\n  - pnpm security:zap          - ZAP scan only\n  - pnpm security:zap:baseline - Docker ZAP baseline scan\n  - pnpm security:zap:api      - Docker ZAP API scan\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review comments for Phase 7 session hardening\n\nThis commit addresses all 19 PR review comments:\n\nCORS & API Gateway:\n- Add X-Client-Fingerprint to CORS allowedHeaders (#1)\n\nOAuth Controller:\n- Add TODO for removing refreshToken from URL after MFE migration (#2)\n\nAuth Service Security:\n- Mask email with maskEmailForLog in fingerprint mismatch log (#3)\n- Remove IP from token blacklist details to protect PII (#4)\n- Update cookie JSDoc to reflect path: ''/'' (#6)\n\nCookie Tests:\n- Fix maxAge test to handle env var variations (#5)\n\nSession Activity Provider:\n- Use refs for dev logging to avoid interval recreation (#7)\n\nSession Timeout Warning:\n- Replace manual focus trap with useFocusTrap hook (#8)\n\nAPI Client Interceptors:\n- Make fingerprint header async with ensureFingerprintHeader (#9)\n\nuseSessionActivity Hook:\n- Store callbacks in refs to avoid effect recreation (#10, #16)\n- Add eslint-disable comment explaining config exclusion\n\nSession Activity Monitor:\n- Fix formatTimeRemaining to use singular \"1 second\" (#11)\n- Handle structural config changes with restart in updateConfig (#12, #19)\n- Fix timeout broadcast storm with timeoutFromRemote flag (#13)\n- Fix unused variable in throttle test (#18)\n\nSession Fingerprint:\n- Fix timezone offset to use proper HH:MM format (e.g., UTC+05:30) (#14)\n- Fix msMaxTouchPoints non-null assertion with nullish coalescing (#15)\n- Remove unused timezone initial value (#17)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review comments for Phase 7 session hardening\n\n- Add try/catch to handleTimeout in SessionActivityProvider to prevent\n  unhandled promise rejections from async logout\n- Fix aria-live announcements in SessionTimeoutWarning: use aria-live=\"off\"\n  on timer display and add separate sr-only span that announces only\n  every 30 seconds or in last 10 seconds to avoid verbosity\n- Don''t cache empty fingerprints in interceptors to allow retry on\n  subsequent requests if initial fingerprint generation fails\n- Fix set -e arithmetic issue in security-test.sh by using $((PASSED + 1))\n  instead of ((PASSED++)) which is incompatible with errexit\n- Use FINGERPRINT variable in security test instead of hardcoded value\n- Fix PORT assignment in security-scan.yml with case statement\n- Update ZAP action versions to v0.15.0 and v0.10.0\n- Add label existence checking before issue creation in security workflow\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address additional PR review comments for security testing\n\n- Re-throw non-404 errors in security-scan.yml label checking loop\n  to fail fast on network/permission issues instead of silently ignoring\n- Change default BASE_URL and API_URL to HTTP in security-test.sh\n  for compatibility with local/CI runs that serve over plain HTTP\n- Remove unused RUN_QUICK variable from security-test.sh main()\n  as quick tests always run (only ZAP is conditional on --full flag)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpjl99CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXt4QAAE11sepyFMklQdCf21WGaLg\n8v+pf+GWI29FWE2urL42K64Q+kDiNNq3LSO7FV9QtMhVclXZ942kxt+XrQbaA1Ww\nDzZ3xL3ghA5ZcIiX0NMhhT/zTlQdTS0GoDm5kOBEG6SE9EzY41hegPQ2hzJAwu1X\nmriYWYWBt3OD25OHIYc9C2pspT5ZtBvGbSC1Ez9SJNBozXuuaHrLaQDNHoxZn0wh\n7f+RR5JQuN2Kp+LBEWoWCVDai9HIqgCMd+Ja/72a/ljcruLH7XJj84v00kCpy5zO\nNtWEvIn9BmYrq9yNpY3tOFdDiot4hLYwvkm+fi28E467CCEyAnZtW/x93mpHVQ0d\n8QnQh0wkphDr6Iqv7hdYyUazuN6b9arhZ1LNVHpMC7FYI7xhuzqfnGXLRcEWm5yY\ny8w4PpVhr+ZBZ10kJS1jEM/Tg1koqN9dTlXozT5c13QXPJAtjzhfVt1c9w8J8N6A\ncYmslE9ZchaQBN3jpL/P+Wp5ZxXIW8URIFwcjR0FePgSOUSOba8EElu2/Rrd3Qp+\nd8Jdqnls3HQMvcgQNDjHH51au3+uVewjLKk1eWhJfK0KGUE3RjEH1uf62sW9l5b5\n0A345yXz7wJmaLfG5+JgAp1xyCEVKFaHJTgC3yarBYFrWC47AFyOQE+WO5/63tGt\nogFfxlkrp9wh5o1CS1YQ\n=jx58\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-12T23:17:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commit/080b6427144b041dedcb0676cef3d0085c18c96f","node_id":"C_kwDOQjNucdoAKDA4MGI2NDI3MTQ0YjA0MWRlZGNiMDY3NmNlZjNkMDA4NWMxOGM5NmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commit/8bb85b0647efdeaefd854cd6efe65dec0da2ab4e","sha":"8bb85b0647efdeaefd854cd6efe65dec0da2ab4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/8bb85b0647efdeaefd854cd6efe65dec0da2ab4e"}],"sha":"080b6427144b041dedcb0676cef3d0085c18c96f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/080b6427144b041dedcb0676cef3d0085c18c96f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/810357?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pateatlau","id":810357,"login":"pateatlau","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDM1Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/8bb85b0647efdeaefd854cd6efe65dec0da2ab4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-12T17:00:56Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Laldingliana Tlau Vantawl"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-12T17:00:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): Phase 6 - Module Federation Security Hardening (#81)\n\n* feat(security): Phase 6 Task 6.1 - SRI Hash Generation for Module Federation\n\nImplement Subresource Integrity (SRI) verification for Module Federation\nremotes to prevent MITM attacks and detect tampered remote entries.\n\nImplementation:\n- Add SRI hash generation script (scripts/security/generate-sri-hashes.js)\n  - Generates SHA-384 hashes for all remoteEntry.js files\n  - Creates dist/sri-manifest.json with hashes and metadata\n  - Generates TypeScript constants for compile-time usage\n  - New npm scripts: build:remotes:sri, security:sri\n\n- Add SecureRemoteLoader utility (libs/shared-utils)\n  - verifyRemoteIntegrity() - Verifies remote content against expected hash\n  - SecureRemoteLoader class - Full-featured loader with caching\n  - URL allowlist validation (blocks unauthorized origins)\n  - Security event logging for audit trail\n  - Configurable: strictMode, allowedOrigins, fetchTimeout\n\n- Add comprehensive test suite (19 tests)\n  - Hash mismatch detection (tampered content)\n  - URL blocking for unauthorized origins\n  - Network error and timeout handling\n  - Security event emission\n\nUsage:\n```typescript\nimport { verifyRemoteIntegrity } from ''@mfe/shared-utils'';\nconst result = await verifyRemoteIntegrity(''authMfe'', remoteUrl);\n```\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(security): Phase 6 Task 6.2 - Remote URL Validation for Module Federation\n\nAdd comprehensive URL validation for Module Federation remotes to prevent\nloading from unauthorized origins and block malicious URL patterns.\n\nImplementation:\n- Add RemoteUrlValidator class with configurable allowlists\n- Validate URLs against origin and path patterns\n- Support wildcard matching for origins (http://localhost:*) and paths (/mfe/*/remoteEntry.js)\n- Block dangerous URL patterns (javascript:, data:, file:, credentials)\n- Environment-aware defaults (stricter HTTPS-only in production)\n- rspack config validation helper for build-time checks\n\nFeatures:\n- Origin allowlist with wildcard support\n- Path pattern matching (glob-style)\n- Protocol enforcement\n- Dangerous pattern blocking\n- Validation result caching\n- Build-time config validation\n\nTest Coverage:\n- 39 tests covering URL validation, pattern matching, edge cases\n- Tests for wildcards, IPv4/IPv6, query strings, custom validators\n\nUsage:\n```typescript\nimport { validateRemoteUrl, RemoteUrlValidator } from ''@mfe/shared-utils'';\n\nconst result = validateRemoteUrl(''http://localhost:4201/remoteEntry.js'');\nconst validator = new RemoteUrlValidator({ allowedOrigins: [''http://localhost''] });\n```\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(security): Phase 6 Task 6.3 - HTTPS Enforcement for Module Federation\n\nAdd production-ready HTTPS enforcement and build-time URL validation\nfor Module Federation remotes.\n\nChanges:\n- Add ALLOWED_REMOTE_ORIGINS configuration with environment-aware defaults\n- Enhance getRemoteUrl() with production HTTPS enforcement\n- Add validateRemoteUrls() for build-time origin validation\n- Add NX_MFE_BASE_URL env var support for custom CDN/server URLs\n- Production builds fail if remote URLs don''t use HTTPS\n- Development builds warn but continue for flexibility\n- Update task list documentation\n\nSecurity Benefits:\n- Prevents man-in-the-middle attacks on remote MFE loading\n- Build-time validation catches configuration errors early\n- Clear audit trail in logs for security review\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(security): Phase 6 Task 6.4 - Remote Fallback Strategy\n\nImplement comprehensive error handling and recovery for Module Federation\nremote loading with retry logic, circuit breaker, and Sentry integration.\n\nChanges:\n- Enhance RemoteErrorBoundary with automatic retries and exponential backoff\n- Add circuit breaker pattern to prevent repeated requests to failing remotes\n- Integrate Sentry for error tracking (breadcrumbs + exception capture)\n- Add loading UI during retry attempts with countdown\n- Show remote name and retry count in error fallback\n- Create circuit-breaker.ts utility with CLOSED/OPEN/HALF_OPEN states\n- Create retry.ts utility with configurable backoff strategy\n\nNew Files:\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/circuit-breaker.ts (22 tests)\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/retry.ts (21 tests)\n\nModified Files:\n- apps/shell/src/components/RemoteErrorBoundary.tsx (16 tests)\n- libs/shared-utils/src/index.ts - Export new utilities\n\nSecurity Benefits:\n- Prevents cascading failures from unavailable remotes\n- Circuit breaker stops repeated requests to failing services\n- Sentry tracking enables quick incident response\n- User-friendly error UI improves UX during outages\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(security): Add comprehensive security validation test suite\n\nAdd integration test suite for validating security configurations:\n- SSL/TLS configuration (certificate validation, protocol versions)\n- nginx security headers (X-Frame-Options, CSP, etc.)\n- Rate limiting (API, Auth, Static endpoints)\n- WebSocket authentication (valid/invalid/expired tokens)\n- Session security (JWT validation, Redis session storage)\n\nUsage: pnpm tsx scripts/security/security-validation.test.ts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(security): Phase 6 Task 6.5 - Remote Health Checks for Module Federation\n\nImplement comprehensive health checking for remote MFEs to identify\nunavailable services early and prevent unnecessary load attempts.\n\nHealth Check Endpoints:\n- Create /health.json endpoint for each MFE (auth, payments, admin, profile)\n- Each endpoint returns: status, name, version, timestamp, components\n\nHealth Check Utilities (libs/shared-utils):\n- checkRemoteHealth() - Check single MFE health with circuit breaker\n- checkAllRemotesHealth() - Check all MFEs in parallel\n- getAggregatedHealthStatus() - Get combined health status\n- preloadHealthCheck() - Shell pre-load health check\n- isRemoteHealthy() - Quick check via circuit breaker state\n- Configurable timeout, degraded status handling\n\nShell Integration:\n- Pre-load health check on app initialization (non-blocking)\n- createRemoteComponent() factory with circuit breaker integration\n- Skip loading unhealthy remotes (circuit breaker OPEN)\n- Return fallback UI when remote is unavailable\n\nMonitoring Components:\n- RemoteHealthStatus - Full health status display\n- RemoteHealthBadge - Compact status indicator\n- useRemoteHealth() hook with optional polling\n- useSingleRemoteHealth() for individual MFE monitoring\n\nTest Coverage:\n- 17 unit tests for health check utilities\n- Tests cover all health states, circuit breaker integration, timeouts\n\nFiles Changed:\n- apps/*/public/health.json - Health endpoints for each MFE\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/remote-health-check.ts - Health utilities\n- apps/shell/src/bootstrap.tsx - Pre-load health check\n- apps/shell/src/remotes/index.tsx - Circuit breaker integration\n- apps/shell/src/components/RemoteHealthStatus.tsx - Monitoring UI\n- apps/shell/src/hooks/useRemoteHealth.ts - React hooks\n\nPhase 6 Progress: 71% (5/7 tasks complete)\nOverall Progress: 83% (35/42 tasks complete)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(security): Phase 6 Task 6.6 - Audit Shared Dependencies for Security\n\nAudit and fix shared dependency configurations across all MFEs to ensure\nsecurity-critical libraries are properly configured as singletons.\n\nIssues Found and Fixed:\n- Auth MFE: Added missing @mfe/shared-api-client and shared-types\n- Admin MFE: Added missing @mfe/shared-api-client and shared-types\n- Profile MFE: Added missing @mfe/shared-api-client and shared-types\n\nSecurity Analysis:\n- All MFEs now have matching singleton configurations for:\n  - shared-auth-store (CRITICAL: auth state management)\n  - @mfe/shared-api-client (CRITICAL: token management)\n  - shared-types (type consistency)\n  - shared-session-sync (cross-tab synchronization)\n  - shared-websocket (WebSocket connection)\n  - @mfe/shared-theme-store (theme state)\n\nDocumentation Created:\n- MODULE-FEDERATION-SHARED-DEPENDENCIES-SECURITY.md\n  - Complete security model documentation\n  - Data flow analysis for authentication\n  - Potential data leak vectors and mitigations\n  - Verification checklist for build/runtime\n  - Recommendations for Phase 7 (Session & Auth Hardening)\n\nFiles Modified:\n- apps/auth-mfe/rspack.config.js\n- apps/admin-mfe/rspack.config.js\n- apps/profile-mfe/rspack.config.js\n- docs/POC-3-Implementation/FRONTEND-MFE-HARDENING-TASK-LIST.md\n\nPhase 6 Progress: 86% (6/7 tasks complete)\nOverall Progress: 86% (36/42 tasks complete)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(security): Phase 6 Task 6.7 - Module Federation Security Testing\n\nComplete comprehensive security test suite for Module Federation:\n\nTest Coverage (276 tests - all passing):\n- URL Validation: 12 tests (allowlist, wildcards, dangerous patterns)\n- Circuit Breaker: 10 tests (state transitions, per-remote isolation)\n- Health Checks: 17 tests (endpoint config, circuit integration)\n- Retry Logic: 6 tests (exponential backoff, max attempts)\n- Security Edge Cases: 6 tests (path traversal, concurrent access)\n\nFiles created:\n- libs/shared-utils/src/lib/module-federation-security.spec.ts\n- docs/POC-3-Implementation/MODULE-FEDERATION-SECURITY-TEST-RESULTS.md\n\nPhase 6 Module Federation Security: 100% Complete (7/7 tasks)\nOverall Progress: 88% (37/42 tasks)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(lint): Remove unused imports in test files\n\nFixed ESLint errors for unused imports:\n- circuit-breaker.spec.ts: Removed unused CircuitState import\n- module-federation-security.spec.ts: Removed unused ValidationResult, isRemoteHealthy imports\n- RemoteErrorBoundary.test.tsx: Removed unused act import\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(shell): Fix TypeScript errors in RemoteErrorBoundary and remotes\n\n- Import ErrorInfo from React for correct callback type\n- Make remoteName prop optional with default value ''unknown''\n- Use ''export type'' for type re-export (isolatedModules compatibility)\n- Simplify createRemoteComponent generic to accept any component props\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(shell): Move eslint-disable comment to correct line\n\nThe eslint-disable-next-line comment needs to be directly above\nthe line containing the violation, not above the function declaration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): Address PR review comments for Module Federation Security\n\nSecurity fixes:\n- Fix origin validation spoofing vulnerability (rspack.config.js, secure-remote-loader.ts)\n  - Replace startsWith with strict hostname comparison\n  - Prevent attacks like localhost.evil.com matching localhost\n- Fix loadSRIManifest retry logic with sentinel flag\n- Fix calculateSHA384 to return proper result when crypto unavailable\n- Fix REMOTE_INTEGRITY_HASHES type annotation for proper RemoteName union\n\nComponent fixes:\n- Fix RemoteErrorBoundary handleReset premature success recording\n  - Move success recording to recovery detection effect\n  - Add circuit breaker guard to handleManualRetry\n- Fix lazy factory to reject instead of resolving with fallback\n  - Allows React.lazy to retry on future mounts\n  - Create RemoteLoadError class for error identification\n\nAccessibility fixes:\n- Add ARIA live regions to RetryingFallback status text\n- Add ARIA live region to circuit status indicator\n- Add role and aria-live to ErrorFallback component\n\nOther fixes:\n- Add public folder copy to admin-mfe rspack config\n- Fix remote-health-check timeout cleanup using finally block\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(types): Fix TypeScript build errors in secure-remote-loader\n\n- Add ''crypto_unavailable'' to RemoteSecurityEvent type union\n- Destructure strictMode from options with default value\n- Convert null to undefined for actualHash (null coalescing)\n- Fix getRemoteIntegrityHash to use type guard for const object indexing\n- Update generate-sri-hashes.js template with same fix\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2899e5e41127b4d7cc9b3a1d3322e5d1c054cc37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/git/trees/2899e5e41127b4d7cc9b3a1d3322e5d1c054cc37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/git/commits/8bb85b0647efdeaefd854cd6efe65dec0da2ab4e","verification":{"payload":"tree 2899e5e41127b4d7cc9b3a1d3322e5d1c054cc37\nparent ec1d93ec6f875ec10e164a768235c3138f5ca2a9\nauthor Laldingliana Tlau Vantawl <pateatlau@gmail.com> 1770915656 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770915656 +0530\n\nfeat(security): Phase 6 - Module Federation Security Hardening (#81)\n\n* feat(security): Phase 6 Task 6.1 - SRI Hash Generation for Module Federation\n\nImplement Subresource Integrity (SRI) verification for Module Federation\nremotes to prevent MITM attacks and detect tampered remote entries.\n\nImplementation:\n- Add SRI hash generation script (scripts/security/generate-sri-hashes.js)\n  - Generates SHA-384 hashes for all remoteEntry.js files\n  - Creates dist/sri-manifest.json with hashes and metadata\n  - Generates TypeScript constants for compile-time usage\n  - New npm scripts: build:remotes:sri, security:sri\n\n- Add SecureRemote