I5NzQ3MThkZDEyMGY3MWQwMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commit/d6fe76023a870298d4bca816f37d5515a993cb62","sha":"d6fe76023a870298d4bca816f37d5515a993cb62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/d6fe76023a870298d4bca816f37d5515a993cb62"}],"sha":"6a7bbc76e9fa5f0aa3735b974718dd120f71d02c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/6a7bbc76e9fa5f0aa3735b974718dd120f71d02c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/810357?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pateatlau","id":810357,"login":"pateatlau","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDM1Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/d6fe76023a870298d4bca816f37d5515a993cb62/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-10T03:32:54Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Laldingliana Tlau Vantawl"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-10T03:32:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Phase 2 and 3 of accessibility implementation completed (#60)\n\n* feat(a11y): complete heading hierarchy audit and add jsx-a11y ESLint plugin\n\nWCAG 2.1 AA Compliance - Priority 1.6 Complete\n\n## Heading Hierarchy Fixes\n\n- Header: Changed branding from <h1> to <span> to prevent multiple h1s\n- Auth MFE: Updated CardTitle to use as=\"h1\" for page titles\n  - SignIn, SignUp, ForgotPassword, ResetPassword, VerificationPending\n- Profile MFE: Fixed heading hierarchy\n  - LinkedAccounts: CardTitle as=\"h2\", h4→h3 for sub-sections\n  - MfaSettings: All CardTitle as=\"h2\", h4→h3 for sub-sections\n\n## ESLint jsx-a11y Configuration\n\n- Installed eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y for compile-time accessibility checks\n- Added 23 accessibility rules covering:\n  - alt-text, heading-has-content, aria-* validation\n  - label-has-associated-control, no-autofocus\n  - interactive-supports-focus, no-static-element-interactions\n\n## Heading Hierarchy per Page\n\n- Sign In/Up: h1 (card title)\n- Payments: h1 (page) → h2 (modal)\n- Profile: h1 (page) → h2 (cards) → h3 (sub-sections)\n- Admin: h1 (dashboard) → h2 (sections)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): resolve jsx-a11y lint warnings and improve accessibility\n\n## JSX-A11Y Fixes\n\n- PaymentsPage: Add keyboard handler and role to modal overlay\n- ToastContext: Add keyboard support and ARIA role to toast wrapper\n- AuditLogs: Convert Label to dl/dt/dd for display-only content\n- SystemHealth: Associate label with select via htmlFor/id\n- PaymentFilters: Use fieldset/legend for grouped inputs, fix date range\n- PaymentDetails: Convert visual-only labels to spans\n- PreferencesForm: Use fieldset/legend for notifications group\n- SkipLink.test: Narrow eslint-disable to only needed rule\n\n## ESLint Configuration\n\n- Configure label-has-associated-control to recognize custom components\n- Add eslint-disable for Label component (used with htmlFor at usage site)\n\n## Theme Token Fixes\n\n- PaymentFilters: text-red-600 → text-destructive\n- PreferencesForm: text-red-600 → text-destructive\n\n## Remaining Intentional Warnings\n\n- autoFocus on auth forms (4 warnings) - UX decision for login flows\n- no-console in backend services - expected for logging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(a11y): implement focus trap for modal dialogs\n\n- Create reusable useFocusTrap hook in shared-utils library\n- Apply focus trap to UserFormDialog, DeleteConfirmDialog, and AuditLogs modal\n- Refactor PaymentsPage modal to use shared useFocusTrap hook\n- Add proper ARIA attributes (role, aria-modal, aria-labelledby, aria-describedby)\n- Support Escape key to close modals and click-outside dismiss\n- Auto-focus first focusable element and restore focus on close\n- Add comprehensive tests for useFocusTrap hook (16 test cases)\n- Update Jest configs for admin-mfe and payments-mfe module mapping\n\nPriority 2.1 of WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility implementation complete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(a11y): improve data table accessibility for WCAG 2.1 AA\n\nTables updated:\n- AuditLogs: Add aria-label, caption, scope=\"col\", live region for pagination\n- UserManagement: Add aria-label, caption, scope=\"col\", descriptive button labels\n- PaymentTable: Add aria-label, caption, scope=\"col\", empty state role\n- PaymentTableRow: Add aria-hidden to icons, descriptive aria-labels with context\n\nImprovements:\n- All table headers now have scope=\"col\" for proper cell-header association\n- Tables have aria-label and visually hidden captions for screen readers\n- Pagination controls wrapped in <nav> with aria-label and live region\n- Action buttons include context (user name, payment amount) in aria-labels\n- Icon buttons have aria-hidden=\"true\" on decorative SVGs\n- Button groups use role=\"group\" with descriptive labels\n- Updated tests to use regex matchers for new descriptive button labels\n\nPriority 2.2 of WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility implementation complete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): update completion status for priorities 2.1 and 2.2\n\nMark the following accessibility priorities as complete in the plan:\n- Focus Management & Trapping (Priority 2.1)\n- Data Table Accessibility (Priority 2.2)\n- Modal/Dialog Accessibility (Priority 2.1)\n\nAdded detailed implementation notes documenting:\n- useFocusTrap hook with 16 unit tests\n- All modals updated with focus trap and ARIA attributes\n- 4 tables updated with proper accessibility (scope, captions, aria-labels)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(a11y): fix color contrast for WCAG 2.1 AA compliance\n\nPriority 2.3: Color Contrast Audit & Fixes\n\nChanges:\n- Light mode: Changed border/input from gray-200 to gray-500 (4.83:1)\n- Light mode: Changed destructive from red-500 to red-700 (6.47:1)\n- Dark mode: Changed border/input from gray-700 to gray-400 (6.99:1)\n- Dark mode: Changed destructive from red-500 to red-600 (4.83:1)\n\nNew files:\n- scripts/contrast-audit.ts: Automated contrast checker script\n- docs/COLOR-CONTRAST-GUIDELINES.md: Color usage guidelines\n- libs/shared-test-utils/src/lib/contrast-test-utils.ts: Testing utilities\n- libs/shared-test-utils/src/lib/contrast-test-utils.spec.ts: 78 unit tests\n\nUpdated MFE styles:\n- apps/shell/src/styles.css\n- apps/admin-mfe/src/styles.css\n- apps/auth-mfe/src/styles.css\n- apps/payments-mfe/src/styles.css\n- apps/profile-mfe/src/styles.css\n\nRun contrast audit: pnpm test:a11y:contrast\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(a11y): add accessible loading states for WCAG 2.1 AA compliance\n\nPriority 2.4 implementation:\n\n- Loading component: Added role=\"status\", aria-busy, aria-live,\n  aria-label, and useAnnounce integration for screen reader announcements\n- Skeleton component: Added role=\"status\", aria-busy, and aria-label\n  for loading placeholder accessibility\n- Button component: Added loading prop with spinner, loadingText,\n  aria-busy, and aria-disabled for accessible loading states\n\nTest updates:\n- Added 15 tests for Loading component accessibility\n- Added 10 tests for Skeleton component accessibility\n- Added 7 loading-specific tests for Button component\n- Updated accessibility.spec.tsx to handle multiple live regions\n- Fixed Jest module mapping for @mfe/shared-utils\n\nAll 214 shared-design-system tests passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(a11y): add comprehensive E2E accessibility test suite\n\nAdd 6 E2E accessibility test files in apps/shell-e2e/src/a11y/:\n- auth-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: Sign In/Up, form labels, keyboard nav\n- payments-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: Table a11y, modal focus trap\n- admin-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: Tab nav, dialogs, audit logs\n- profile-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: Form validation, preferences\n- keyboard-navigation.spec.ts: Skip links, no traps, focus order\n- screen-reader.spec.ts: ARIA live regions, landmarks, headings\n\nTests verify WCAG 2.1 AA compliance using @axe-core/playwright with\ncomprehensive keyboard navigation and ARIA attribute verification.\n\nNPM scripts added:\n- test:e2e:a11y:auth, :payments, :admin, :profile\n- test:e2e:a11y:keyboard, :screen-reader\n- test:e2e:a11y:all\n\nCompletes Priority 3.1 of the Accessibility Compliance Plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): add comprehensive accessibility documentation\n\nCreate docs/ACCESSIBILITY-GUIDELINES.md with:\n- WCAG 2.1 AA key principles and requirements\n- Component accessibility patterns (buttons, forms, modals, tables)\n- Color contrast guidelines with approved color palette\n- Keyboard navigation and screen reader support patterns\n- Testing checklists (automated and manual)\n- Development workflow and code examples\n- ARIA reference\n\nUpdate CLAUDE.md with:\n- Accessibility section with key requirements\n- Testing commands for all a11y tests\n- Modal and form patterns with examples\n- References to shared utilities\n\nCompletes Priority 3.2 of the Accessibility Compliance Plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): add comprehensive screen reader testing guide\n\nCreate docs/SCREEN-READER-TESTING-GUIDE.md with:\n- VoiceOver (macOS) setup and essential commands\n- NVDA (Windows) installation and commands\n- 8 detailed testing scenarios covering all MFEs:\n  * Sign In flow (form labels, validation)\n  * Payments table (structure, headers, actions)\n  * Modal dialogs (focus trap, escape, restoration)\n  * Form validation (required, errors, aria-invalid)\n  * Tab navigation (roles, selection, panels)\n  * Live region announcements (form submission)\n  * Navigation landmarks (page structure)\n  * Loading states (announcements)\n- Common issues and solutions\n- Testing checklist (pre-test, per-page, cross-page)\n- Issue severity levels and reporting template\n\nEach scenario includes VoiceOver/NVDA test steps, expected\nannouncements (verbatim), and pass criteria.\n\nCompletes Priority 3.3 of the Accessibility Compliance Plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tests): resolve Jest module resolution for @mfe/shared-utils\n\n- Add @mfe/shared-utils to moduleNameMapper in all Jest configs\n- Fix admin-mfe Loading component test to use getByLabelText\n- Prevents module resolution errors when Loading component uses useAnnounce\n\nThis resolves CI test failures in profile-mfe, auth-mfe, and admin-mfe.\nShell tests have pre-existing failures unrelated to this fix.\n\n* fix(lint): resolve TypeScript unused variable errors\n\n- Fix JSX closing tag in AuditLogs.tsx (nav -> /nav)\n- Remove unused ''index'' parameter in AuditLogs map\n- Prefix unused ''key'' parameters with underscore in contrast-test-utils\n\nAll linting errors resolved. Only warnings remain.\n\n* fix(tests): update AuditLogs test to use getByLabelText for Loading\n\nSame fix as UserManagement - use getByLabelText instead of getByRole\nto avoid ambiguity with useAnnounce''s global live regions.\n\n* fix(lint): resolve unused variable errors in E2E test files\n\nPrefix all unused variables with underscore in accessibility E2E tests:\n- auth-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: ariaInvalid, alerts, errorVisible, errors\n- keyboard-navigation.spec.ts: loginAsAdmin (eslint disable), initialValue, newValue\n- payments-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: errors, ariaLabel, ariaCurrent\n- profile-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: hasError, initialValue, alerts, errorIndicators\n- screen-reader.spec.ts: assertiveAnnouncer, hasErrorMechanism, statusMessages,\n  emailRequired, passwordRequired, invalidFields, ariaBusy, disabled, ariaDisabled,\n  currentCount, ariaLabel, liveRegions, decorativeSvgs, announcer\n\nAll linting errors resolved. Only console warnings remain.\n\n* fix(build): add @mfe/shared-utils module resolution for TypeScript and Rspack\n\n- Add @mfe/shared-utils to tsconfig.base.json paths\n- Add @mfe/shared-utils alias to all rspack.config.js files (shell, auth, payments, admin, profile)\n- Fix Loading component className prop reference (was using props.className after destructuring)\n- Fix useFocusTrap return type (remove redundant | null from RefObject)\n- Add optional chaining to focus() calls in useFocusTrap for strict null checks\n\nResolves build errors:\n- TS2307: Cannot find module ''@mfe/shared-utils''\n- TS2339: Property ''className'' does not exist\n- TS18048: ''firstFocusable''/''lastFocusable'' is possibly ''undefined''\n- TS2322: RefObject type not assignable to LegacyRef\n\n* fix(a11y): address PR review comments (items 1-6)\n\n1. Fix AuditLogs.tsx definition list structure - move closing </dl> after conditional blocks\n2. Update contrast ratio comments in auth-mfe/styles.css (4.8:1 and 7:1)\n3. Fix PaymentTable.tsx ARIA - replace aria-label with aria-labelledby/describedby\n4. Document dark-mode token limitations in COLOR-CONTRAST-GUIDELINES.md\n5. Add useCallback wrappers for onEscape handlers (PaymentsPage, AuditLogs)\n6. Fix moduleNameMapper regex in shared-design-system/jest.config.cts\n\nThese fixes improve accessibility semantics, prevent unnecessary re-renders,\nand ensure proper documentation of color contrast limitations.\n\n* fix(a11y): address PR review comments (items 7-12)\n\n7. Add className assertion to Loading.test.tsx\n8. Restore heading semantics in shared-header-ui (span -> h1)\n9. Fix sRGB threshold in contrast-test-utils (0.03928 -> 0.04045)\n12. Handle asChild prop in Button component (warn if used)\n\nThese fixes improve test coverage, accessibility semantics, WCAG compliance,\nand prevent invalid DOM attributes.\n\n* fix(a11y): address PR review comments - stability, types, and keyboard\n\n- Button.tsx: Destructure asChild prop and add console warning\n- useFocusTrap: Add TypeScript imports, use ref for onEscape stability\n- useFocusTrap: Add RAF cleanup to prevent memory leaks\n- useFocusTrap: Improve auto-focus test assertion\n- ToastContext: Add Space key handler for button role\n- contrast-audit.ts: Update shebang to tsx and fix run instructions\n- contrast-audit.ts: Fix sRGB threshold (0.03928 → 0.04045)\n\nAll changes address PR review comments for accessibility compliance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(e2e): add visibility assertions before click actions\n\nProfile Flow Tests:\n- Add visibility checks before clicking navigation links\n- Verify elements are visible before interacting with them\n- Add assertions after form submissions to verify success\n- Improve tab switching assertions\n\nDark Mode Tests:\n- Add visibility checks before clicking theme toggle buttons\n- Ensure theme toggle is visible before activation\n- Fix conditional click assertions\n\nThese changes improve test reliability by verifying elements\nare visible and ready for interaction before performing actions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(shared-utils): fix useFocusTrap auto-focus test\n\nFixed test that was creating two separate hook instances instead\nof reusing the same instance. The test now correctly:\n- Renders hook once with isActive: false\n- Assigns container ref\n- Rerenders with isActive: true to trigger auto-focus\n- Verifies first button receives focus\n\nThis ensures the auto-focus behavior is properly tested.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"035753dcd0a6fbace74d46ca1449d052d81f6302","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/git/trees/035753dcd0a6fbace74d46ca1449d052d81f6302"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/git/commits/d6fe76023a870298d4bca816f37d5515a993cb62","verification":{"payload":"tree 035753dcd0a6fbace74d46ca1449d052d81f6302\nparent 99b3609b4a741eb853bb56452571eb45b3bea892\nauthor Laldingliana Tlau Vantawl <pateatlau@gmail.com> 1770694374 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770694374 +0530\n\nPhase 2 and 3 of accessibility implementation completed (#60)\n\n* feat(a11y): complete heading hierarchy audit and add jsx-a11y ESLint plugin\n\nWCAG 2.1 AA Compliance - Priority 1.6 Complete\n\n## Heading Hierarchy Fixes\n\n- Header: Changed branding from <h1> to <span> to prevent multiple h1s\n- Auth MFE: Updated CardTitle to use as=\"h1\" for page titles\n  - SignIn, SignUp, ForgotPassword, ResetPassword, VerificationPending\n- Profile MFE: Fixed heading hierarchy\n  - LinkedAccounts: CardTitle as=\"h2\", h4→h3 for sub-sections\n  - MfaSettings: All CardTitle as=\"h2\", h4→h3 for sub-sections\n\n## ESLint jsx-a11y Configuration\n\n- Installed eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y for compile-time accessibility checks\n- Added 23 accessibility rules covering:\n  - alt-text, heading-has-content, aria-* validation\n  - label-has-associated-control, no-autofocus\n  - interactive-supports-focus, no-static-element-interactions\n\n## Heading Hierarchy per Page\n\n- Sign In/Up: h1 (card title)\n- Payments: h1 (page) → h2 (modal)\n- Profile: h1 (page) → h2 (cards) → h3 (sub-sections)\n- Admin: h1 (dashboard) → h2 (sections)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): resolve jsx-a11y lint warnings and improve accessibility\n\n## JSX-A11Y Fixes\n\n- PaymentsPage: Add keyboard handler and role to modal overlay\n- ToastContext: Add keyboard support and ARIA role to toast wrapper\n- AuditLogs: Convert Label to dl/dt/dd for display-only content\n- SystemHealth: Associate label with select via htmlFor/id\n- PaymentFilters: Use fieldset/legend for grouped inputs, fix date range\n- PaymentDetails: Convert visual-only labels to spans\n- PreferencesForm: Use fieldset/legend for notifications group\n- SkipLink.test: Narrow eslint-disable to only needed rule\n\n## ESLint Configuration\n\n- Configure label-has-associated-control to recognize custom components\n- Add eslint-disable for Label component (used with htmlFor at usage site)\n\n## Theme Token Fixes\n\n- PaymentFilters: text-red-600 → text-destructive\n- PreferencesForm: text-red-600 → text-destructive\n\n## Remaining Intentional Warnings\n\n- autoFocus on auth forms (4 warnings) - UX decision for login flows\n- no-console in backend services - expected for logging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(a11y): implement focus trap for modal dialogs\n\n- Create reusable useFocusTrap hook in shared-utils library\n- Apply focus trap to UserFormDialog, DeleteConfirmDialog, and AuditLogs modal\n- Refactor PaymentsPage modal to use shared useFocusTrap hook\n- Add proper ARIA attributes (role, aria-modal, aria-labelledby, aria-describedby)\n- Support Escape key to close modals and click-outside dismiss\n- Auto-focus first focusable element and restore focus on close\n- Add comprehensive tests for useFocusTrap hook (16 test cases)\n- Update Jest configs for admin-mfe and payments-mfe module mapping\n\nPriority 2.1 of WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility implementation complete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(a11y): improve data table accessibility for WCAG 2.1 AA\n\nTables updated:\n- AuditLogs: Add aria-label, caption, scope=\"col\", live region for pagination\n- UserManagement: Add aria-label, caption, scope=\"col\", descriptive button labels\n- PaymentTable: Add aria-label, caption, scope=\"col\", empty state role\n- PaymentTableRow: Add aria-hidden to icons, descriptive aria-labels with context\n\nImprovements:\n- All table headers now have scope=\"col\" for proper cell-header association\n- Tables have aria-label and visually hidden captions for screen readers\n- Pagination controls wrapped in <nav> with aria-label and live region\n- Action buttons include context (user name, payment amount) in aria-labels\n- Icon buttons have aria-hidden=\"true\" on decorative SVGs\n- Button groups use role=\"group\" with descriptive labels\n- Updated tests to use regex matchers for new descriptive button labels\n\nPriority 2.2 of WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility implementation complete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): update completion status for priorities 2.1 and 2.2\n\nMark the following accessibility priorities as complete in the plan:\n- Focus Management & Trapping (Priority 2.1)\n- Data Table Accessibility (Priority 2.2)\n- Modal/Dialog Accessibility (Priority 2.1)\n\nAdded detailed implementation notes documenting:\n- useFocusTrap hook with 16 unit tests\n- All modals updated with focus trap and ARIA attributes\n- 4 tables updated with proper accessibility (scope, captions, aria-labels)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(a11y): fix color contrast for WCAG 2.1 AA compliance\n\nPriority 2.3: Color Contrast Audit & Fixes\n\nChanges:\n- Light mode: Changed border/input from gray-200 to gray-500 (4.83:1)\n- Light mode: Changed destructive from red-500 to red-700 (6.47:1)\n- Dark mode: Changed border/input from gray-700 to gray-400 (6.99:1)\n- Dark mode: Changed destructive from red-500 to red-600 (4.83:1)\n\nNew files:\n- scripts/contrast-audit.ts: Automated contrast checker script\n- docs/COLOR-CONTRAST-GUIDELINES.md: Color usage guidelines\n- libs/shared-test-utils/src/lib/contrast-test-utils.ts: Testing utilities\n- libs/shared-test-utils/src/lib/contrast-test-utils.spec.ts: 78 unit tests\n\nUpdated MFE styles:\n- apps/shell/src/styles.css\n- apps/admin-mfe/src/styles.css\n- apps/auth-mfe/src/styles.css\n- apps/payments-mfe/src/styles.css\n- apps/profile-mfe/src/styles.css\n\nRun contrast audit: pnpm test:a11y:contrast\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(a11y): add accessible loading states for WCAG 2.1 AA compliance\n\nPriority 2.4 implementation:\n\n- Loading component: Added role=\"status\", aria-busy, aria-live,\n  aria-label, and useAnnounce integration for screen reader announcements\n- Skeleton component: Added role=\"status\", aria-busy, and aria-label\n  for loading placeholder accessibility\n- Button component: Added loading prop with spinner, loadingText,\n  aria-busy, and aria-disabled for accessible loading states\n\nTest updates:\n- Added 15 tests for Loading component accessibility\n- Added 10 tests for Skeleton component accessibility\n- Added 7 loading-specific tests for Button component\n- Updated accessibility.spec.tsx to handle multiple live regions\n- Fixed Jest module mapping for @mfe/shared-utils\n\nAll 214 shared-design-system tests passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(a11y): add comprehensive E2E accessibility test suite\n\nAdd 6 E2E accessibility test files in apps/shell-e2e/src/a11y/:\n- auth-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: Sign In/Up, form labels, keyboard nav\n- payments-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: Table a11y, modal focus trap\n- admin-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: Tab nav, dialogs, audit logs\n- profile-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: Form validation, preferences\n- keyboard-navigation.spec.ts: Skip links, no traps, focus order\n- screen-reader.spec.ts: ARIA live regions, landmarks, headings\n\nTests verify WCAG 2.1 AA compliance using @axe-core/playwright with\ncomprehensive keyboard navigation and ARIA attribute verification.\n\nNPM scripts added:\n- test:e2e:a11y:auth, :payments, :admin, :profile\n- test:e2e:a11y:keyboard, :screen-reader\n- test:e2e:a11y:all\n\nCompletes Priority 3.1 of the Accessibility Compliance Plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): add comprehensive accessibility documentation\n\nCreate docs/ACCESSIBILITY-GUIDELINES.md with:\n- WCAG 2.1 AA key principles and requirements\n- Component accessibility patterns (buttons, forms, modals, tables)\n- Color contrast guidelines with approved color palette\n- Keyboard navigation and screen reader support patterns\n- Testing checklists (automated and manual)\n- Development workflow and code examples\n- ARIA reference\n\nUpdate CLAUDE.md with:\n- Accessibility section with key requirements\n- Testing commands for all a11y tests\n- Modal and form patterns with examples\n- References to shared utilities\n\nCompletes Priority 3.2 of the Accessibility Compliance Plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(a11y): add comprehensive screen reader testing guide\n\nCreate docs/SCREEN-READER-TESTING-GUIDE.md with:\n- VoiceOver (macOS) setup and essential commands\n- NVDA (Windows) installation and commands\n- 8 detailed testing scenarios covering all MFEs:\n  * Sign In flow (form labels, validation)\n  * Payments table (structure, headers, actions)\n  * Modal dialogs (focus trap, escape, restoration)\n  * Form validation (required, errors, aria-invalid)\n  * Tab navigation (roles, selection, panels)\n  * Live region announcements (form submission)\n  * Navigation landmarks (page structure)\n  * Loading states (announcements)\n- Common issues and solutions\n- Testing checklist (pre-test, per-page, cross-page)\n- Issue severity levels and reporting template\n\nEach scenario includes VoiceOver/NVDA test steps, expected\nannouncements (verbatim), and pass criteria.\n\nCompletes Priority 3.3 of the Accessibility Compliance Plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tests): resolve Jest module resolution for @mfe/shared-utils\n\n- Add @mfe/shared-utils to moduleNameMapper in all Jest configs\n- Fix admin-mfe Loading component test to use getByLabelText\n- Prevents module resolution errors when Loading component uses useAnnounce\n\nThis resolves CI test failures in profile-mfe, auth-mfe, and admin-mfe.\nShell tests have pre-existing failures unrelated to this fix.\n\n* fix(lint): resolve TypeScript unused variable errors\n\n- Fix JSX closing tag in AuditLogs.tsx (nav -> /nav)\n- Remove unused ''index'' parameter in AuditLogs map\n- Prefix unused ''key'' parameters with underscore in contrast-test-utils\n\nAll linting errors resolved. Only warnings remain.\n\n* fix(tests): update AuditLogs test to use getByLabelText for Loading\n\nSame fix as UserManagement - use getByLabelText instead of getByRole\nto avoid ambiguity with useAnnounce''s global live regions.\n\n* fix(lint): resolve unused variable errors in E2E test files\n\nPrefix all unused variables with underscore in accessibility E2E tests:\n- auth-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: ariaInvalid, alerts, errorVisible, errors\n- keyboard-navigation.spec.ts: loginAsAdmin (eslint disable), initialValue, newValue\n- payments-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: errors, ariaLabel, ariaCurrent\n- profile-mfe.a11y.spec.ts: hasError, initialValue, alerts, errorIndicators\n- screen-reader.spec.ts: assertiveAnnouncer, hasErrorMechanism, statusMessages,\n  emailRequired, passwordRequired, invalidFields, ariaBusy, disabled, ariaDisabled,\n  currentCount, ariaLabel, liveRegions, decorativeSvgs, announcer\n\nAll linting errors resolved. Only console warnings remain.\n\n* fix(build): add @mfe/shared-utils module resolution for TypeScript and Rspack\n\n- Add @mfe/shared-utils to tsconfig.base.json paths\n- Add @mfe/shared-utils alias to all rspack.config.js files (shell, auth, payments, admin, profile)\n- Fix Loading component className prop reference (was using props.className after destructuring)\n- Fix useFocusTrap return type (remove redundant | null from RefObject)\n- Add optional chaining to focus() calls in useFocusTrap for strict null checks\n\nResolves build errors:\n- TS2307: Cannot find module ''@mfe/shared-utils''\n- TS2339: Property ''className'' does not exist\n- TS18048: ''firstFocusable''/''lastFocusable'' is possibly ''undefined''\n- TS2322: RefObject type not assignable to LegacyRef\n\n* fix(a11y): address PR review comments (items 1-6)\n\n1. Fix AuditLogs.tsx definition list structure - move closing </dl> after conditional blocks\n2. Update contrast ratio comments in auth-mfe/styles.css (4.8:1 and 7:1)\n3. Fix PaymentTable.tsx ARIA - replace aria-label with aria-labelledby/describedby\n4. Document dark-mode token limitations in COLOR-CONTRAST-GUIDELINES.md\n5. Add useCallback wrappers for onEscape handlers (PaymentsPage, AuditLogs)\n6. Fix moduleNameMapper regex in shared-design-system/jest.config.cts\n\nThese fixes improve accessibility semantics, prevent unnecessary re-renders,\nand ensure proper documentation of color contrast limitations.\n\n* fix(a11y): address PR review comments (items 7-12)\n\n7. Add className assertion to Loading.test.tsx\n8. Restore heading semantics in shared-header-ui (span -> h1)\n9. Fix sRGB threshold in contrast-test-utils (0.03928 -> 0.04045)\n12. Handle asChild prop in Button component (warn if used)\n\nThese fixes improve test coverage, accessibility semantics, WCAG compliance,\nand prevent invalid DOM attributes.\n\n* fix(a11y): address PR review comments - stability, types, and keyboard\n\n- Button.tsx: Destructure asChild prop and add console warning\n- useFocusTrap: Add TypeScript imports, use ref for onEscape stability\n- useFocusTrap: Add RAF cleanup to prevent memory leaks\n- useFocusTrap: Improve auto-focus test assertion\n- ToastContext: Add Space key handler for button role\n- contrast-audit.ts: Update shebang to tsx and fix run instructions\n- contrast-audit.ts: Fix sRGB threshold (0.03928 → 0.04045)\n\nAll changes address PR review comments for accessibility compliance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(e2e): add visibility assertions before click actions\n\nProfile Flow Tests:\n- Add visibility checks before clicking navigation links\n- Verify elements are visible before interacting with them\n- Add assertions after form submissions to verify success\n- Improve tab switching assertions\n\nDark Mode Tests:\n- Add visibility checks before clicking theme toggle buttons\n- Ensure theme toggle is visible before activation\n- Fix conditional click assertions\n\nThese changes improve test reliability by verifying elements\nare visible and ready for interaction before performing actions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(shared-utils): fix useFocusTrap auto-focus test\n\nFixed test that was creating two separate hook instances instead\nof reusing the same instance. The test now correctly:\n- Renders hook once with isActive: false\n- Assigns container ref\n- Rerenders with isActive: true to trigger auto-focus\n- Verifies first button receives focus\n\nThis ensures the auto-focus behavior is properly tested.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpiqbmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfJYQAFGCSfo+6aPCGQTIV+1Mr6lb\nP5K6OY/JGqIch1BY3oogOvTkr/n8EiIOmJHztjy96UUK0/1/6hy39cCBdHPYzE39\nfN3KQIydPFDQQaZV2sVh6dmcy2sjw/UjzRveobJKDJphbMy3HZKb4RzSdzcp2PYt\nioQq+BeWslULwk64C7t/4gYkq4At3Rf4MNJgzZQQuwbU25wMd5IWUHte/zzDTw/T\niS3hrLr3MisBv+sCY2CGsYbUdzJjlSGCgK0SbfcIXslPtHXcVLo7qm5MamsikLKQ\nY4l9rNIBSWPyF/uei8d814m