s://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/407f3febb132a0e637877f524ff828b2a43d1a06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-09T07:14:42Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Patea Tlau"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-09T07:14:42Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Patea Tlau"},"message":"fix(ci): prevent OOM by running shell tests without coverage\n\nThe CI pipeline was failing with JavaScript heap OOM during Jest coverage\ncollection. Root cause: Shell app as Module Federation host imports many\nfederated modules, causing Istanbul coverage instrumentation to consume\n8GB+ memory (exceeding GitHub runner''s 7GB RAM).\n\nChanges:\n- Split shell tests from coverage collection in CI workflow\n- Shell tests now run without --coverage flag\n- Reduced NODE_OPTIONS from 8192MB to 4096MB (safe for 7GB runners)\n- Added --forceExit to prevent hanging on open handles\n- Fixed test assertion failures (min-h-screen → min-h-full)\n- Added static asset mocking for PNG imports in Jest config\n- Added MemoryRouter wrapper to AdminPage tests\n\nShell app is primarily an integration point - business logic coverage\ncomes from individual MFEs and shared libraries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d241dd944f8ac4b20002bd047f83ff05e9d3376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/git/trees/3d241dd944f8ac4b20002bd047f83ff05e9d3376"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/git/commits/407f3febb132a0e637877f524ff828b2a43d1a06","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verifie