/api.github.com/users/pateatlau/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/commits/9aebfaa57adfa70fac27beae3db397059849f990/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-24T16:06:55Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Patea Tlau"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-24T16:06:55Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Patea Tlau"},"message":"docs(i18n): add comprehensive Hindi language implementation plan\n\nAdd detailed i18n implementation plan for Hindi (hi-IN) as the second\nsupported language after English (en-IN). The plan covers:\n\n- react-i18next setup with Module Federation singleton configuration\n- Translation file structure with 6 namespaces (common, auth, payments,\n  admin, profile, validation)\n- Complete English and Hindi translations for all MFE components\n- Language switcher component with persistence\n- Backend i18n middleware for Accept-Language header\n- API response localization with localized error messages\n- User language preference storage in database\n- E2E testing fixtures for multiple locales\n- CI/CD translation validation with coverage thresholds\n- Hindi-specific considerations (Devanagari script, pluralization)\n- Future RTL language support preparation\n\n4 phases, 17 priorities, ~44 hours estimated effort.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"76ffc7e2d0d44e98b9f9a9ea31f71cc11761425e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/git/trees/76ffc7e2d0d44e98b9f9a9ea31f71cc11761425e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/payments-system-mfe-microservices-fullstack-nx-2026/git/commits/9aebfaa57adfa70fac27beae3db397059849f990","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"http