kages\n\nPHASE 2 COMPLETION - Enterprise Infrastructure:\n\n1. @medi-aide/database-migrations Package:\n   - Enterprise-grade TypeORM migration utilities\n   - Migration locking to prevent concurrent runs\n   - Checksum validation for integrity\n   - Audit trail for compliance (HIPAA/SOC2)\n   - Automatic rollback on failure\n   - BaseMigration class with idempotent helpers\n   - Safe table/column/index existence checks\n\n2. @medi-aide/kafka-client Package:\n   - Type-safe event publishing with Zod validation\n   - Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) support\n   - Automatic retry with exponential backoff\n   - Prometheus metrics integration\n   - Consumer group management\n   - Graceful shutdown handling\n   - Event envelope with correlation IDs\n   - Health check indicators\n\n3. @medi-aide/temporal-worker Package:\n   - Production-ready Temporal worker\n   - Activity implementations for all workflows\n   - Connection retry with backoff\n   - Prometheus metrics endpoint\n   - Health check endpoint\n   - Graceful shutdown handling\n   - Activity metrics tracking\n\n4. @medi-aide/service-auth Package (Enhanced):\n   - JWT token generation and validation\n   - Token caching for performance\n   - Scope-based authorization\n   - Service allowlist support\n   - NestJS guard with decorators\n   - Authenticated HTTP client\n   - @Public, @RequireScopes, @AllowServices decorators\n   - @CallingService parameter decorator\n\nENTERPRISE FEATURES:\n- All packages include Prometheus metrics\n- Health check integration with @nestjs/terminus\n- Graceful shutdown handling\n- Retry policies with exponential backoff\n- Comprehensive logging\n- Type-safe with full TypeScript support\n\nNEXT STEPS (Phase 3):\n- Set up CI/CD pipeline\n- Configure Grafana dashboards\n- Enable distributed tracing\n- Kubernetes migration preparation","tree":{"sha":"105aa89c68b3fd0ff19d90029b8baf907b2408a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/medi-platform/medi-aide-microservices/git/trees/105aa89c68b3fd0ff19d90029b8