"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/b494b98968fabc5694074c3b9c1c983327eeb663","node_id":"C_kwDOQkVc4doAKGI0OTRiOTg5NjhmYWJjNTY5NDA3NGMzYjljMWM5ODMzMjdlZWI2NjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/51134476fd6809e6da63bd8fbdd5f80685fd204b","sha":"51134476fd6809e6da63bd8fbdd5f80685fd204b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/51134476fd6809e6da63bd8fbdd5f80685fd204b"}],"sha":"b494b98968fabc5694074c3b9c1c983327eeb663","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/b494b98968fabc5694074c3b9c1c983327eeb663"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nzeckets","id":80357080,"login":"nzeckets","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzU3MDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/51134476fd6809e6da63bd8fbdd5f80685fd204b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T01:08:51Z","email":"80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nick Zeckets"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T01:08:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Sync PLATFORM.md: two rules on exposing a product to AI agents (#39)\n\nBrings this copy in line with the other product repos (PLATFORM.md is\nmeant to be the same file everywhere, section 15).\n\n- Rule 37 gains a note that Throughline ships the same operations\n  registry architecture as SocialOS, with a sixth risk class (replace)\n  and the per-token limit in a migrated RateLimitBucket table.\n- New rule 41: a machine token must not inherit the web''s staff god\n  mode. Throughline''s userCanAccessOrg answers yes for any platform\n  admin, so its token path checks real membership and admits another\n  tenant only when the token names it, flagged staffGrant.\n- New rule 42: a \"read\" helper that creates on first read is a write.\n  Throughline''s plan report created a draft plan on read, and campaign\n  analytics fired a background HubSpot refresh; a static call-graph\n  audit now fails on any reachable write or vendor call from a read op.\n\nCopies that were behind also pick up the MoltSets email-lookup detail\non the Throughline and SocialOS send-email handoff.\n\nDocs only.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Zeckets <nick@smokesignals.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"005e7ee0dd16d30697b6ffcfec0f523ce788cd22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/005e7ee0dd16d30697b6ffcfec0f523ce788cd22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/51134476fd6809e6da63bd8fbdd5f80685fd204b","verification":{"payload":"tree 005e7ee0dd16d30697b6ffcfec0f523ce788cd22\nparent 800c727f933db18bdd1ecf09851fe5b0c9cedc7a\nauthor Nick Zeckets <80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com> 1790557731 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790557731 -0400\n\nSync PLATFORM.md: two rules on exposing a product to AI agents (#39)\n\nBrings this copy in line with the other product repos (PLATFORM.md is\nmeant to be the same file everywhere, section 15).\n\n- Rule 37 gains a note that Throughline ships the same operations\n  registry architecture as SocialOS, with a sixth risk class (replace)\n  and the per-token limit in a migrated RateLimitBucket table.\n- New rule 41: a machine token must not inherit the web''s staff god\n  mode. Throughline''s userCanAccessOrg answers yes for any platform\n  admin, so its token path checks real membership and admits another\n  tenant only when the token names it, flagged staffGrant.\n- New rule 42: a \"read\" helper that creates on first read is a write.\n  Throughline''s plan report created a draft plan on read, and campaign\n  analytics fired a background HubSpot refresh; a static call-graph\n  audit now fails on any reachable write or vendor call from a read op.\n\nCopies that were behind also pick up the MoltSets email-lookup detail\non the Throughline and SocialOS send-email handoff.\n\nDocs only.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Zeckets <nick@smokesignals.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqub4jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbl4QADm/DJIi/crVADX7rS0hzPJ7\n3mbYsOsDeaVAo8pbPfNG1GJ6cG0pO7/PnQdhxmx8USoO77+ss8+5bmqby40B3d7k\n2VS699ywDaYUuAISYjolUQqCy5/BXGRvM7aLW/SMnVar7OoGQPB1KWDmkyK0Dzti\n04u0mE+fbCYE9xjcDbluVviz7QicLFfvAdrU1HHqPHCUZSpDhqdwb1zO46xPJhI1\n+Bx/GHQ/uwj4RO5LB3NLCeW/PY7x2UxRImTADd65Mnwb7EMGPZaf07emuRd873S8\nN4NRkrEfY14IDQyerMz7wpEDJGlL46W4lMP3TQplKa1TdUG0tPA2T0cTG6cTZiss\nNmTeavvCCys/p1rOhF00xQ0ZOa9ll038qtklL2i0IM6iL9mJ+1hGWQPwyZYhqgyW\nluHQ1i8FTGaVRNZSD7x3Dl38Qb0x4AW9+PnMc1xNNBaxZLvPDqp4ZOpPVBGcQZgT\nf3WVIHN+yI0NjRKaLUgGd5HOZIRTPnIAL8tlsGcMSpnIJcojBSHQyf/WVjadnEYZ\nsphDbuaGHjOHc/D56BLhR29ChjBTWNhNrVLlkh/eUd8mpJCioCzc20wwjcr73Gvj\nzE4z6eSC7bZd6+An9zL4hqF5KQDXlBB57r6ba1lVRdU48q2QsHAJ38wGm6lcRr8K\nonOqS3fDjy8cSMk/YY5b\n=tMKM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T01:08:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.gith