https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/2c3c2d4e671c7e1a6795914115f84cf44211633c","node_id":"C_kwDOQkVc4doAKDJjM2MyZDRlNjcxYzdlMWE2Nzk1OTE0MTE1Zjg0Y2Y0NDIxMTYzM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/600328eb1b5de4b01f2f111e6838bca8b354be3f","sha":"600328eb1b5de4b01f2f111e6838bca8b354be3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/600328eb1b5de4b01f2f111e6838bca8b354be3f"}],"sha":"2c3c2d4e671c7e1a6795914115f84cf44211633c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/2c3c2d4e671c7e1a6795914115f84cf44211633c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nzeckets","id":80357080,"login":"nzeckets","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzU3MDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/600328eb1b5de4b01f2f111e6838bca8b354be3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T13:42:26Z","email":"80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nick Zeckets"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T13:42:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Backfill ICP grades for all submissions that predate the grading feature (#35)\n\n* Add \"what they do\" company summary to the ICP sales notification\n\nThe grade >= C sales ping (from #33) tells sales who submitted and how they\nscored, but not what the company does — the rep still had to open the\nreport or the website to find out. Add a one-line summary sourced from the\nLinkedIn company description (usually the cleanest self-description),\nfalling back to the site''s own meta description. Bounded at 280 chars,\ncut on a word boundary, omitted entirely when neither source has text.\n\nVerified with a stubbed-Slack formatting test: line present and bounded on\nlong input, absent on empty input.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\n* Backfill ICP grades for all submissions that predate the grading feature\n\nRuns the same evaluator as live traffic (services/icp.js) over every\ncontact with a submitted website and writes gtmos_icp_grade/_detail:\n\n- usesHubSpot comes from gtmos_crm (portal-wide re-verified 2026-07-09);\n  contacts with no verdict are re-probed now, and still-unreachable sites\n  are left ungraded rather than stamped F on missing data.\n- Headcount/description via fresh LinkedIn company lookup by domain\n  (cached); title from the contact''s jobtitle plus the stored analysis''\n  headline when Redis still has it; the paid classifier runs only for\n  HubSpot-positive contacts, same as the live path.\n- No Slack notifications: a historical bulk pass must not flood #sales.\n- Idempotent: already-graded contacts are skipped, so organic grades are\n  never overwritten and interrupted runs resume cleanly.\n- Writes grades directly instead of via pushIcpGrade, which re-runs\n  ensureProperties per call (3x API traffic over a 190-contact loop);\n  ensureProperties runs once at startup instead.\n\nDry-run by default; --apply to write.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f84bad1188a4bdb5b39ae9e4dd364eb326257a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/f84bad1188a4bdb5b39ae9e4dd364eb326257a07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/600328eb1b5de4b01f2f111e6838bca8b354be3f","verification":{"payload":"tree f84bad1188a4bdb5b39ae9e4dd364eb326257a07\nparent 0e205d07ec42d06ac8085f7ebe9d27a579c5b2e8\nauthor Nick Zeckets <80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com> 1783690946 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783690946 -0400\n\nBackfill ICP grades for all submissions that predate the grading feature (#35)\n\n* Add \"what they do\" company summary to the ICP sales notification\n\nThe grade >= C sales ping (from #33) tells sales who submitted and how they\nscored, but not what the company does — the rep still had to open the\nreport or the website to find out. Add a one-line summary sourced from the\nLinkedIn company description (usually the cleanest self-description),\nfalling back to the site''s own meta description. Bounded at 280 chars,\ncut on a word boundary, omitted entirely when neither source has text.\n\nVerified with a stubbed-Slack formatting test: line present and bounded on\nlong input, absent on empty input.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\n* Backfill ICP grades for all submissions that predate the grading feature\n\nRuns the same evaluator as live traffic (services/icp.js) over every\ncontact with a submitted website and writes gtmos_icp_grade/_detail:\n\n- usesHubSpot comes from gtmos_crm (portal-wide re-verified 2026-07-09);\n  contacts with no verdict are re-probed now, and still-unreachable sites\n  are left ungraded rather than stamped F on missing data.\n- Headcount/description via fresh LinkedIn company lookup by domain\n  (cached); title from the contact''s jobtitle plus the stored analysis''\n  headline when Redis still has it; the paid classifier runs only for\n  HubSpot-positive contacts, same as the live path.\n- No Slack notifications: a historical bulk pass must not flood #sales.\n- Idempotent: already-graded contacts are skipped, so organic grades are\n  never overwritten and interrupted runs resume cleanly.\n- Writes grades directly instead of via pushIcpGrade, which re-runs\n  ensureProperties per call (3x API traffic over a 190-contact loop);\n  ensureProperties runs once at startup instead.\n\nDry-run by default; --apply to write.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUPbCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiYYQAF60r3mT5ixhUMxSmPnKi/Ol\nomEh5dnyBtZP3uZ01VQ/M6AJ2UV3W8Wj/qp0rGnVL/nTRixbNA+a8uxxQdpvqHwj\noaHADTxIU+wA+xVJPPGRK+TGaHYmnt9B3J9wyb6o3RP7bJjoxDcdIC5febQW72Vs\nEh