205d07ec42d06ac8085f7ebe9d27a579c5b2e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/0e205d07ec42d06ac8085f7ebe9d27a579c5b2e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nzeckets","id":80357080,"login":"nzeckets","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzU3MDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/c2c300c49cf127debd11f72efa6084cca21df87f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T22:41:44Z","email":"80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nick Zeckets"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T22:41:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ICP grading: score every submission A/B/C/F, write to HubSpot, ping sales (#33)\n\nGrades each submission per sales'' rules (services/icp.js):\n- F: no HubSpot detected on their site, or the company is a HubSpot/\n  growth/marketing agency (Haiku classifier reads the scraped website).\n- C: has HubSpot + not an agency (floor for a pass; <10 employees or\n  unknown headcount stays here).\n- B: 10-25 employees. A: more than 25.\n- Title adjusts downward only: below director caps at B; unknown title\n  demotes one level (never below C); director+ changes nothing.\nWhether the company''s buyers live on LinkedIn is captured as an\ninformational signal only.\n\nThe grade lands in a new gtmos_icp_grade dropdown (A/B/C/F, created by\nensureProperties — the portal has no existing grade property) with the\naudit trail in gtmos_icp_grade_detail. Any submission grading C or\nbetter notifies the sales channel (SLACK_SALES_CHANNEL_ID, default\n#sales). Grade write + notification hang off the scoring promise, not\nreport completion, so a visitor who abandons the page mid-generation is\nstill graded and still reaches sales.\n\nScoring is best-effort throughout: classifier trouble falls back to\ndeterministic title keywords and LinkedIn headcount parsing, and missing\ndata never fails anyone.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VSwZ5xAod7HTeiJ1eH6hGa\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7192646c95a68a065f4944e8fa074c6f91903547","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/7192646c95a68a065f4944e8fa074c6f91903547"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/c2c300c49cf127debd11f72efa6084cca21df87f","verification":{"payload":"tree 7192646c95a68a065f4944e8fa074c6f91903547\nparent 9870e7ce8eb209ebf609116c91d920beca1a365a\nauthor Nick Zeckets <80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com> 1783636904 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783636904 -0400\n\nICP grading: score every submission A/B/C/F, write to HubSpot, ping sales (#33)\n\nGrades each submission per sales'' rules (services/icp.js):\n- F: no HubSpot detected on their site, or the company is a HubSpot/\n  growth/marketing agency (Haiku classifier reads the scraped website).\n- C: has HubSpot + not an agency (floor for a pass; <10 employees or\n  unknown headcount stays here).\n- B: 10-25 employees. A: more than 25.\n- Title adjusts downward only: below director caps at B; unknown title\n  demotes one level (never below C); director+ changes nothing.\nWhether the company''s buyers live on LinkedIn is captured as an\ninformational signal only.\n\nThe grade lands in a new gtmos_icp_grade dropdown (A/B/C/F, created by\nensureProperties — the portal has no existing grade property) with the\naudit trail in gtmos_icp_grade_detail. Any submission grading C or\nbetter notifies the sales channel (SLACK_SALES_CHANNEL_ID, default\n#sales). Grade write + notification hang off the scoring promise, not\nreport completion, so a visitor who abandons the page mid-generation is\nstill graded and still reaches sales.\n\nScoring is best-effort throughout: classifier trouble falls back to\ndeterministic title keywords and LinkedIn headcount parsing, and missing\ndata never fails anyone.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VSwZ5xAod7HTeiJ1eH6hGa\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUCOoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1UAQAEtP4w3rfJDICNkrS29VqD0R\n1g/AkSxjt8bbz+VKu210yzhRwOCr+x3ZuRZmHNPI4EhYFufkXlAMNocorG269zEB\nLfJiTIv5WkkvRBuTw6NZfOvvVr5+WWY+t5JkZ97kFihKp3D9b2t9x/IpJWuqz5by\n7C0l89Z1RgAWwDzQVVr3ACa/3EYRh1kpKy4blXCXic8tOuiSq7G8cT0skys0/3RX\n+kDqPZxS9WcgbgJc60LIJduKGepkJJMcfdgEMTUR3zBU3CZwltjc5SJGfn1NX22E\nlg3fHtdLPeBOtgoyujOCNGodEN6piTeK0b5J3VyOG3JInIhwL+QacM9P4LIxsx/B\nPZRYCbw1cVMItyUMOPjD+5sHftsDgMNXyUD5BH4VNAi5p9Oec4FRUrW27uQFDnkn\nFs9cv3PrFZOS1tIEGpw9e0c6M93QVFul9m/QimWDzNVojAq4vo5aJ6lVKrmF9KkV\necVPMtZ6RHaTgbrsmUAjjosdlAvqJCteDyK0GUZAnpynvesy+QnSnU+XAbTEM6HO\nhquZfcZk9HgOvHppvetGXx206+oj+sgckMULxh+ygd3ZDSrhxNqet++HeFd6g7s+\nUEOky7lBu2lorstJwvgVrZ/wyC11Q/FkovMZPozbiKo7YEye8hrRq5yLd5Qz8pwS\nx6v7ex7WmGquRyuuFnpV\n=d9nM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-09T22:41:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/c2c300c49cf127debd11f72efa6084cca21df87f","node_id":"C_kwDOQkVc4doAKGMyYzMwMGM0OWNmMTI3ZGViZDExZjcyZWZhNjA4NGNjYTIxZGY4N2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/9870e7ce8eb209ebf609116c91d920beca1a365a","sha":"9870e7ce8eb209ebf609116c91d920beca1a365a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/9870e7ce8eb209ebf609116c91d920beca1a365a"}],"sha":"c2c300c49cf127debd11f72efa6084cca21df87f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/c2c300c49cf127debd11f72efa6084cca21df87f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nzeckets","id":80357080,"login":"nzeckets","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzU3MDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/9870e7ce8eb209ebf609116c91d920beca1a365a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T17:35:29Z","email":"80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nick Zeckets"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T17:35:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Definitive HubSpot detection: portal IDs, headers, GTM, Firecrawl fallback (#32)\n\nThe old detection was a bare substring scan over page source, so a blog\npost about HubSpot counted as \"uses HubSpot\" (premium model + wrong\ngtmos_crm) while GTM-injected HubSpot and bot-blocked scrapes counted as\n\"doesn''t\". Replaced with a tiered detector:\n\n- Portal-id patterns (definitive): tracking loader, analytics runtime,\n  forms embeds — extracts the actual portal id, now written to a new\n  gtmos_hubspot_portal_id contact property.\n- Response headers (definitive): HubSpot-CMS-hosted sites answer with\n  x-powered-by: HubSpot; fetchPage now surfaces headers.\n- Asset references (strong): hubspot-owned hosts in src/href/url() only;\n  prose mentions no longer count.\n- GTM container follow-up: when raw HTML shows GTM but no HubSpot, fetch\n  the public gtm.js and scan it for the tags it injects.\n\nScraper upgrades:\n- Real browser UA (the self-identifying bot UA was exactly what\n  bot-blockers filter).\n- Optional Firecrawl fallback (FIRECRAWL_API_KEY): when the plain fetch is\n  blocked or the page is a client-rendered shell, render-scrape through\n  Firecrawl for both research text and detection surface. Self-disables\n  without a key.\n- /contact added to the subpage list (where HubSpot forms usually live).\n- probeHubSpot() export: single-site detection probe for scripts.\n\nscripts/regrade-hubspot-detection.js re-probes every submission on record\n(contacts with gtmos_website_url + analyses still in Redis) and corrects\ngtmos_crm / portal id / the stored usesHubSpot flag. Unreachable sites are\nleft untouched; dry-run by default.\n\nVerified with behavioral tests: portal-id extraction, forms embeds,\nprose-mention rejection, header detection, GTM-container follow-up,\nunreachable-site neutrality, contact-page forms.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ad26743e4b95b56af60835849416398ec9a45110","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/ad26743e4b95b56af60835849416398ec9a45110"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/9870e7ce8eb209ebf609116c91d920beca1a365a","verification":{"payload":"tree ad26743e4b95b56af60835849416398ec9a45110\nparent 823a5a30691f44a27decb63532d72585dd806d91\nauthor Nick Zeckets <80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com> 1783618529 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783618529 -0400\n\nDefinitive HubSpot detection: portal IDs, headers, GTM, Firecrawl fallback (#32)\n\nThe old detection was a bare substring scan over page source, so a blog\npost about HubSpot counted as \"uses HubSpot\" (premium model + wrong\ngtmos_crm) while GTM-injected HubSpot and bot-blocked scrapes counted as\n\"doesn''t\". Replaced with a tiered detector:\n\n- Portal-id patterns (definitive): tracking loader, analytics runtime,\n  forms embeds — extracts the actual portal id, now written to a new\n  gtmos_hubspot_portal_id contact property.\n- Response headers (definitive): HubSpot-CMS-hosted sites answer with\n  x-powered-by: HubSpot; fetchPage now surfaces headers.\n- Asset references (strong): hubspot-owned hosts in src/href/url() only;\n  prose mentions no longer count.\n- GTM container follow-up: when raw HTML shows GTM but no HubSpot, fetch\n  the public gtm.js and scan it for the tags it injects.\n\nScraper upgrades:\n- Real browser UA (the self-identifying bot UA was exactly what\n  bot-blockers filter).\n- Optional Firecrawl fallback (FIRECRAWL_API_KEY): when the plain fetch is\n  blocked or the page is a client-rendered shell, render-scrape through\n  Firecrawl for both research text and detection surface. Self-disables\n  without a key.\n- /contact added to the subpage list (where HubSpot forms usually live).\n- probeHubSpot() export: single-site detection probe for scripts.\n\nscripts/regrade-hubspot-detection.js re-probes every submission on record\n(contacts with gtmos_website_url + analyses still in Redis) and corrects\ngtmos_crm / portal id / the stored usesHubSpot flag. Unreachable sites are\nleft untouched; dry-run by default.\n\nVerified with behavioral tests: portal-id extraction, forms embeds,\nprose-mention rejection, header detection, GTM-container follow-up,\nunreachable-site neutrality, contact-page forms.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT9vhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGYYQAGCygV909mhqRKvE+DEtRxxh\nef7ONkVtBs7FYJh2G8Pmb/Yixqox8vlxzdUx6lUV5Ln8hEYbO5Llq9+5kDZGrfBR\n7+GS9Qe6JUndxWr6G8BArKAMP2+8WEI4xeY6U2CePZjyQzbbF+tuC5vScazjOs7I\nT9mydCU+g7SBFzHMyORtWrbMpBCglNJKsL6VkWvaejeaLDiOngpat7g4QAXM0+Kd\ncX4Yl2ThOf08pCi3rfgD9lEQPA2BeU10BjkvJcuXQMUjnBoqL6UWuBCGUpiSFHyu\nJRVv38pgy4mxMXQC7kwZTkgx0PGGNds33pp+HQnfsjPrrvctVwC0WXzhQK7gSKLi\nXiKbuN5j/Po2UTz0ieQJkc62sQd1spQkHPmGRAV0nNsE+gzBxDjqFn6JGVpkjUXu\nHqf3T8nnAkVkuBvbUTGuin2FQco9cdSLzCj3lnoCL2Gcvm71DSqZSg3qymkLeBLd\nRE/RDqt7z3xKvoU7Xh3VebIJ9Ev41O+APPdZYl+eLLWxhZ/G3YRba5ju3HFnpQsa\nUQKi6KpmSueWtJY1DHkfKgTn3HrNzNJ9wh7JaKbIlG+G/N19FSiEkbnT9q4w4QZY\nEMPY8DiJN8KKjjq5xRKOB90VVtbl8mJZNy9NNu+2h+TAgQpaF4HktspTIZN+nexZ\n6ehF0jDFQXNW5t2zuzt7\n=2wf6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-09T17:35:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/9870e7ce8eb209ebf609116c91d920beca1a365a","node_id":"C_kwDOQkVc4doAKDk4NzBlN2NlOGViMjA5ZWJmNjA5MTE2YzkxZDkyMGJlY2ExYTM2NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/823a5a30691f44a27decb63532d72585dd806d91","sha":"823a5a30691f44a27decb63532d72585dd806d91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/823a5a30691f44a27decb63532d72585dd806d91"}],"sha":"9870e7ce8eb209ebf609116c91d920beca1a365a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/9870e7ce8eb209ebf609116c91d920beca1a365a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nzeckets","id":80357080,"login":"nzeckets","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzU3MDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/823a5a30691f44a27decb63532d72585dd806d91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T16:11:35Z","email":"80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nick Zeckets"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T16:11:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Coerce enrichment fields to strings: object-valued company 400s HubSpot creates (#31)\n\nThe Anysite API sometimes returns experience fields as nested objects\n(company: {name, urn, ...}) and enrichPersonByEmail passed them through\nuntouched, so enrichedPerson.company reached HubSpot''s contact create as a\nJSON object and the whole create 400''d (\"Cannot deserialize value of type\njava.lang.String\"). Those visitors got their report but no CRM record —\nthis is still happening in production (contacts missing for July 7-9\nanalyses), and it poisoned 15 of the backfill''s creates.\n\n- anysite.js: textOrName() unwraps object values to their display text for\n  company and title in both enrichment paths, so contact creates (and\n  prompts/Slack, which would have printed [object Object]) always get strings.\n- backfill script: the analyses already stored in Redis carry the object\n  values, so contactProps/linkedinUrl apply the same coercion.\n\nRe-running the backfill recovers the 13 leads whose creates failed; it\nskips everything already written.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f64ad7efda173be624ff1bbbc80acc7898dd9126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/f64ad7efda173be624ff1bbbc80acc7898dd9126"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/823a5a30691f44a27decb63532d72585dd806d91","verification":{"payload":"tree f64ad7efda173be624ff1bbbc80acc7898dd9126\nparent 496b146c4cc076e94e50951496bcd3a1a52fd94a\nauthor Nick Zeckets <80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com> 1783613495 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783613495 -0400\n\nCoerce enrichment fields to strings: object-valued company 400s HubSpot creates (#31)\n\nThe Anysite API sometimes returns experience fields as nested objects\n(company: {name, urn, ...}) and enrichPersonByEmail passed them through\nuntouched, so enrichedPerson.company reached HubSpot''s contact create as a\nJSON object and the whole create 400''d (\"Cannot deserialize value of type\njava.lang.String\"). Those visitors got their report but no CRM record —\nthis is still happening in production (contacts missing for July 7-9\nanalyses), and it poisoned 15 of the backfill''s creates.\n\n- anysite.js: textOrName() unwraps object values to their display text for\n  company and title in both enrichment paths, so contact creates (and\n  prompts/Slack, which would have printed [object Object]) always get strings.\n- backfill script: the analyses already stored in Redis carry the object\n  values, so contactProps/linkedinUrl apply the same coercion.\n\nRe-running the backfill recovers the 13 leads whose creates failed; it\nskips everything already written.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT8g3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADqEQAJHAysDNhg2ZaBt+3JH1AQ2h\nmJJD5AYF1o4XF5W4668tYx/ptS3+4dVxG47KRA8/zzeLskH5nU81G6GyrkOlcgst\nz0KDIuRMvAgOlyTug41kJEiJySrdNZbTMIhNJdNmkI97gmffD6NR27528hsvbqRw\n9HhCPGZcLVeP8gx0hsnxEc7ScO8v04y4m7frIYQoa/4dG2tIOhKxsDO47foR7X3t\nNcexEKCec6Q5UGW7bMQWYl7c6Qhha5utff4TItL6P6ziO6FL8ShN47Dvwuy2iBaU\nitdOlFbseFMq3ErcudHRYnI++1/w7Znx3TIcxg/kIYgdPtc3Ez/lOrA8JJAns56T\nD0zPiOW+1Ks+4xPkzHeYxX4ib+ugBUvelpWMa2ISB0Apxek1JCj75I+WFYqVr43R\nrFXPl9IhEpYQcEQyCYndC8o6FrsHfZqhfcQw4f0v594Kzi6OQw5KzPciYKCn+kqH\nk+VOhgbmvKk8DjJ+IKJbn/vWptdn2ggwqqmddTKItLRjRzLsVUCNqXe5pdTcKQ/L\nSlIpYmyWiGr4FXEhwPvF/V5S59q5iB7J2dZTUkIeupWyh4+qPea/+e/KcUaGVtN8\n3d5uNTtl1k/5oIYU3bQWAy+fS+M8iDYrY3Wa1y+xIVveJLdkznqOFnM22EVAb4u8\n1NYzXssibOwneCggq5hN\n=Jwhf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-09T16:11:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/823a5a30691f44a27decb63532d72585dd806d91","node_id":"C_kwDOQkVc4doAKDgyM2E1YTMwNjkxZjQ0YTI3ZGVjYjYzNTMyZDcyNTg1ZGQ4MDZkOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/496b146c4cc076e94e50951496bcd3a1a52fd94a","sha":"496b146c4cc076e94e50951496bcd3a1a52fd94a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/496b146c4cc076e94e50951496bcd3a1a52fd94a"}],"sha":"823a5a30691f44a27decb63532d72585dd806d91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/823a5a30691f44a27decb63532d72585dd806d91"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nzeckets","id":80357080,"login":"nzeckets","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzU3MDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/496b146c4cc076e94e50951496bcd3a1a52fd94a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T15:56:59Z","email":"80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nick Zeckets"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T15:56:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Backfill: create contacts for leads lost to the June create bug; retry 429s (#30)\n\nThe dry run against production Redis found 39 analyses with no HubSpot\ncontact at all — visitors from ~June 15-29, when new-contact creates were\n400ing (the linkedin_url payload bug fixed in #27). Skipping them loses\nthose leads for good once the Redis TTL expires, so the backfill now\ncreates the contact (standard properties from the stored enrichment, same\nshape as runWorkstreamA) before pushing the analysis.\n\nAlso observed in the dry run: HubSpot''s shared ~5 req/s search limit 429''d\ntwice at a 300ms cadence alongside live app traffic. Searches, creates,\nand pushes now retry on 429 with exponential backoff, and the loop paces\nat 600ms. Invalid emails are skipped via the shared validateEmail.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9d9b69e85c70fb2a46eae00a5b8de9f9a1f562f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/9d9b69e85c70fb2a46eae00a5b8de9f9a1f562f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/496b146c4cc076e94e50951496bcd3a1a52fd94a","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d9b69e85c70fb2a46eae00a5b8de9f9a1f562f7\nparent 0b7e7076f5d606f564682d117ee77b3e1ec493bc\nauthor Nick Zeckets <80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com> 1783612619 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783612619 -0400\n\nBackfill: create contacts for leads lost to the June create bug; retry 429s (#30)\n\nThe dry run against production Redis found 39 analyses with no HubSpot\ncontact at all — visitors from ~June 15-29, when new-contact creates were\n400ing (the linkedin_url payload bug fixed in #27). Skipping them loses\nthose leads for good once the Redis TTL expires, so the backfill now\ncreates the contact (standard properties from the stored enrichment, same\nshape as runWorkstreamA) before pushing the analysis.\n\nAlso observed in the dry run: HubSpot''s shared ~5 req/s search limit 429''d\ntwice at a 300ms cadence alongside live app traffic. Searches, creates,\nand pushes now retry on 429 with exponential backoff, and the loop paces\nat 600ms. Invalid emails are skipped via the shared validateEmail.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT8TLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwawQAFZbzssfXawovqfd2wT9gtq7\n4eO+qqDSgEeYtW3kkEvJvLZ4KyNVN+8QtuwYycLUn/IN7+JIYtxqob4jEPfPQMB4\n3zzTLgp8M/wnQYROV10IuNN36gYTV6A5kZXsRhja3oFvF+HQldj/p8fvHTE/4SbX\nnw0gX49DsltDBak8EwJVuNE/iTa9lCj+onqtLwgSyOGhoAf+SetaRs5Y27SXXU8f\npJbjREnHH9BO6Bj2LIvATVd8SzHHvEazEBYVDkE1Lty7c+BAwkzdEq/bQCixV3+O\ntWkKC6u8N6TRmiIii5U+a0jdPezDYjP8tGvG4akPtLu5KuqAXdHI1h+8LRtoBum1\nQ/XuF9MyV38bfCVQQbQrS884BP3O4OXZv8tS65ewT1cbi1+o+XZkFu/h6mXct6K/\ncxkX8XS/krZptH2seJ0u3wVLu8F2JhcMSc7XabD7D1Gp9XxhhzQkVn/YK8ZlzQKe\nVyq/XTrUdHmuQ5gHRUZGLl+ZQrgKbg033U6smn0Bt0644x8veXC1nqeiryZbEbVe\nzjP+4/uPDLiCff6K1borz/ewnorLxai61Gi59CSSVNnXOSoo0VdY+MGRhlEq/ZEu\nCIRdiwdNi2k7IyHxgiXaCxVuoFCK2oCX6eIqnuaF0qXnBXl1rVLS70WS+3Hj6ODn\nJ3mzE/+gPxAughkyKbsh\n=ERX9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-09T15:57:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/496b146c4cc076e94e50951496bcd3a1a52fd94a","node_id":"C_kwDOQkVc4doAKDQ5NmIxNDZjNGNjMDc2ZTk0ZTUwOTUxNDk2YmNkM2ExYTUyZmQ5NGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/0b7e7076f5d606f564682d117ee77b3e1ec493bc","sha":"0b7e7076f5d606f564682d117ee77b3e1ec493bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/0b7e7076f5d606f564682d117ee77b3e1ec493bc"}],"sha":"496b146c4cc076e94e50951496bcd3a1a52fd94a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/496b146c4cc076e94e50951496bcd3a1a52fd94a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nzeckets","id":80357080,"login":"nzeckets","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzU3MDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/0b7e7076f5d606f564682d117ee77b3e1ec493bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T14:52:44Z","email":"80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nick Zeckets"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T14:52:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix HubSpot lead writes broken by portal property cleanup (#29)\n\nEvery pushAnalysisToContact PATCH has been rejected by HubSpot since\n2026-06-29: the payload included gtmos_linkedin_url, which was deleted in\na portal property cleanup that day, and HubSpot rejects the entire update\nwhen any property in the payload doesn''t exist. Contact creation (standard\nproperties only) kept working, so leads appeared but silently lost their\nreport URL and all analysis data. ensureProperties couldn''t heal it because\nHubSpot reserves archived property names, and the logs only said\n\"HubSpot API error: 400\" with no body.\n\n- Drop gtmos_linkedin_url from the payload and property definitions; write\n  the LinkedIn URL to the standard hs_linkedin_url instead (only when\n  non-empty, so other integrations'' values are never wiped).\n- Align gtmos_completed_at with the portal''s current datetime type and send\n  a full ISO timestamp.\n- Make analysis and shared-report writes self-healing: when HubSpot flags\n  specific properties as invalid, drop just those, retry with the rest, and\n  log loudly which fields are being lost — a portal edit can no longer\n  zero out lead capture.\n- Include the HubSpot response body in error messages so a rejected payload\n  is diagnosable from the logs.\n- Add scripts/backfill-hubspot-analyses.js to reattach the analyses stored\n  in Redis (30-day TTL) to the contacts that missed their write. Dry-run by\n  default, idempotent via the gtmos_completed_at check, rate-limited.\n\nVerified with a stubbed-fetch behavioral test: bad-property drop + retry in\nboth HubSpot 400 shapes, non-property 400 and 401 propagate, linkedin URL\nmapping, ISO datetime format.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3f6d04c26b35052c7b1d8077a14fed026bd3acb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/3f6d04c26b35052c7b1d8077a14fed026bd3acb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/0b7e7076f5d606f564682d117ee77b3e1ec493bc","verification":{"payload":"tree 3f6d04c26b35052c7b1d8077a14fed026bd3acb9\nparent eb98eae95d928530ec80c3b6fbf094792e71a491\nauthor Nick Zeckets <80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com> 1783608764 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783608764 -0400\n\nFix HubSpot lead writes broken by portal property cleanup (#29)\n\nEvery pushAnalysisToContact PATCH has been rejected by HubSpot since\n2026-06-29: the payload included gtmos_linkedin_url, which was deleted in\na portal property cleanup that day, and HubSpot rejects the entire update\nwhen any property in the payload doesn''t exist. Contact creation (standard\nproperties only) kept working, so leads appeared but silently lost their\nreport URL and all analysis data. ensureProperties couldn''t heal it because\nHubSpot reserves archived property names, and the logs only said\n\"HubSpot API error: 400\" with no body.\n\n- Drop gtmos_linkedin_url from the payload and property definitions; write\n  the LinkedIn URL to the standard hs_linkedin_url instead (only when\n  non-empty, so other integrations'' values are never wiped).\n- Align gtmos_completed_at with the portal''s current datetime type and send\n  a full ISO timestamp.\n- Make analysis and shared-report writes self-healing: when HubSpot flags\n  specific properties as invalid, drop just those, retry with the rest, and\n  log loudly which fields are being lost — a portal edit can no longer\n  zero out lead capture.\n- Include the HubSpot response body in error messages so a rejected payload\n  is diagnosable from the logs.\n- Add scripts/backfill-hubspot-analyses.js to reattach the analyses stored\n  in Redis (30-day TTL) to the contacts that missed their write. Dry-run by\n  default, idempotent via the gtmos_completed_at check, rate-limited.\n\nVerified with a stubbed-fetch behavioral test: bad-property drop + retry in\nboth HubSpot 400 shapes, non-property 400 and 401 propagate, linkedin URL\nmapping, ISO datetime format.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KRMY5pPWVyb4u3yFo6tqHG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT7W8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu6oQADAL55T+uZMRM5fP353UOe1j\npHi1kyrJFFNPffWQeekWZY4b9aVBW2wG9bE4Az8JrK8ij1e7jjSmPEDYlHWTx05f\ntD2AyDh19NnZKGasHP0Q5/vDPLc6fWG43rHNEXTg2Ct0DT0QgWxV1ansa6/HP6K5\nuQkaOCITyvFIEGLjQ94XbeXGRuonRJY+tBVEZY7xq8XyP349eBlisR8w5JbWOaHt\nIcmfpEaFaecjwX1WsYvkjfJg4hdeRTXif71Hu7rCkBkZtAMgpIa/yuxrEgvrAXyZ\nZje2H5d8ZGj8m0B1PXWm4bbTMpXzkMaNYErW+Ddx280It2y5kVhbMdFo1pwquWq0\nEtPFywH4LhREKwWRhzNMZZXlgeAxQjIodeERVnTlGekyt4/X5D7dbdw1lUk089xp\naW/mtao1ZAffb2rxSDEXOPPCQm2LynybBQXxWmUi5jsTWmBrDNRublrvr0KXi4Wt\nshBxoQilEve7aOJpu8SPtVoIelkuIGcPoF6wVfUlAst+qJNw/Be9OdyW9eEGdKhI\nWpKBByj8FKkisGY8bdww4909q6H5NT0VZwVKeUdvv0MN+c6CsDkRfDxBEqhhmVTK\nk10tUYAW19A2z+p2Fxwo1J7Vl63JS/AXslgOHh+28EOjHj8ZmFn2ExQBtcbO8NNu\nOEmH22PH2qgHYULIh+CP\n=Tp8z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-09T14:52:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/0b7e7076f5d606f564682d117ee77b3e1ec493bc","node_id":"C_kwDOQkVc4doAKDBiN2U3MDc2ZjVkNjA2ZjU2NDY4MmQxMTdlZTc3YjNlMWVjNDkzYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/eb98eae95d928530ec80c3b6fbf094792e71a491","sha":"eb98eae95d928530ec80c3b6fbf094792e71a491","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/eb98eae95d928530ec80c3b6fbf094792e71a491"}],"sha":"0b7e7076f5d606f564682d117ee77b3e1ec493bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/0b7e7076f5d606f564682d117ee77b3e1ec493bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nzeckets","id":80357080,"login":"nzeckets","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzU3MDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/eb98eae95d928530ec80c3b6fbf094792e71a491/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T21:21:43Z","email":"80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nick Zeckets"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T21:21:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Reliability pass: fix all 24 audit findings (#28)\n\nBackend / infra\n- store.js: in-memory fallback now honors TTL + sweeps (no unbounded growth);\n  add Redis-backed checkRateLimit (durable, shared across replicas) and a\n  health() accessor; warn loudly when REDIS_URL is missing in production. (C1, M6, H5)\n- index.js: global unhandledRejection/uncaughtException handlers (benign socket\n  errors no longer crash the process), Express error middleware, and /health now\n  reports store status. (C2)\n- cache.js: background sweeper; rate-limit logic moved to the store. (M6)\n- analyze.js: SSE heartbeat, client-disconnect abort (AbortController threaded to\n  the model stream), and guarded writes so a dead socket can''t crash the request;\n  rate limit via the durable store; skip the company-profile lookup when nothing\n  resolved (no wasted 412/timeout). (C2, H3, H4, H5, M2)\n- anysite.js: 30s -> 10s per-call timeout (configurable), retries on transient\n  errors only (never 4xx), and stop caching failures as empty for 24h; brief\n  negative cache for company resolves. (C4, H4, L5)\n- anthropic.js: tolerant, order-independent section parser that backfills any\n  missing section so none renders empty in the page/PDF/chat; abort signal\n  support. (H2)\n- prompts/analysis.js: bound chat grounding to ~12k chars. (M4)\n- pdf.js (service): render the micro-app spec as a readable summary instead of\n  dumping raw JSON; proper <ol>/<ul> list handling; strip stray code fences. (H1, M3, M7)\n- pdf.js (route): friendly HTML error pages instead of JSON 500 in a browser tab;\n  per-IP rate limit. (M8, H5)\n- chat.js: Slack reply dedupe is stored and only marked seen AFTER the write\n  succeeds (failed write -> Slack retry recovers it); per-conversation rate limit. (H6, H5)\n- slack.js: keep the thread alive (and its analysis mapping) when the first\n  follow-up post fails. (L4)\n- survey.js: validate email, cap/clean array input, stop masking failures as ok. (L1)\n\nFrontend\n- app.js: handle stream-end-without-result + flush the buffer tail and decoder so\n  a dropped final frame no longer strands the user on the loading screen; stall\n  watchdog + AbortController so a frozen stream surfaces an error; supersede the\n  previous run on retry/resubmit; throttle the O(n^2) transcript re-render;\n  tolerant micro-app + email-sequence parsing; markdown code-fence and generic\n  ''##'' handling; PDF button restores on refocus; idempotent setup; chat-poll\n  backoff. (C3, H3, M1, M5, M7, M9, L2, L3)\n\nVerified: all files syntax-check; section parser, PDF rendering, and store\nrate-limit/TTL covered by behavioral tests.\n\nNOTE: C1 also requires provisioning Redis and setting REDIS_URL in Railway — an\ninfrastructure step the code now supports and surfaces but cannot perform itself.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H6KZ3kfjGQK7SjWKUL2NhM\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"15bc59f4cdc07bfa6f0757408d1ae50314890e17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/15bc59f4cdc07bfa6f0757408d1ae50314890e17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/eb98eae95d928530ec80c3b6fbf094792e71a491","verification":{"payload":"tree 15bc59f4cdc07bfa6f0757408d1ae50314890e17\nparent 233c3d0ee5341d93f97c25ac9cc16f68e9ee789a\nauthor Nick Zeckets <80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com> 1782768103 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782768103 -0400\n\nReliability pass: fix all 24 audit findings (#28)\n\nBackend / infra\n- store.js: in-memory fallback now honors TTL + sweeps (no unbounded growth);\n  add Redis-backed checkRateLimit (durable, shared across replicas) and a\n  health() accessor; warn loudly when REDIS_URL is missing in production. (C1, M6, H5)\n- index.js: global unhandledRejection/uncaughtException handlers (benign socket\n  errors no longer crash the process), Express error middleware, and /health now\n  reports store status. (C2)\n- cache.js: background sweeper; rate-limit logic moved to the store. (M6)\n- analyze.js: SSE heartbeat, client-disconnect abort (AbortController threaded to\n  the model stream), and guarded writes so a dead socket can''t crash the request;\n  rate limit via the durable store; skip the company-profile lookup when nothing\n  resolved (no wasted 412/timeout). (C2, H3, H4, H5, M2)\n- anysite.js: 30s -> 10s per-call timeout (configurable), retries on transient\n  errors only (never 4xx), and stop caching failures as empty for 24h; brief\n  negative cache for company resolves. (C4, H4, L5)\n- anthropic.js: tolerant, order-independent section parser that backfills any\n  missing section so none renders empty in the page/PDF/chat; abort signal\n  support. (H2)\n- prompts/analysis.js: bound chat grounding to ~12k chars. (M4)\n- pdf.js (service): render the micro-app spec as a readable summary instead of\n  dumping raw JSON; proper <ol>/<ul> list handling; strip stray code fences. (H1, M3, M7)\n- pdf.js (route): friendly HTML error pages instead of JSON 500 in a browser tab;\n  per-IP rate limit. (M8, H5)\n- chat.js: Slack reply dedupe is stored and only marked seen AFTER the write\n  succeeds (failed write -> Slack retry recovers it); per-conversation rate limit. (H6, H5)\n- slack.js: keep the thread alive (and its analysis mapping) when the first\n  follow-up post fails. (L4)\n- survey.js: validate email, cap/clean array input, stop masking failures as ok. (L1)\n\nFrontend\n- app.js: handle stream-end-without-result + flush the buffer tail and decoder so\n  a dropped final frame no longer strands the user on the loading screen; stall\n  watchdog + AbortController so a frozen stream surfaces an error; supersede the\n  previous run on retry/resubmit; throttle the O(n^2) transcript re-render;\n  tolerant micro-app + email-sequence parsing; markdown code-fence and generic\n  ''##'' handling; PDF button restores on refocus; idempotent setup; chat-poll\n  backoff. (C3, H3, M1, M5, M7, M9, L2, L3)\n\nVerified: all files syntax-check; section parser, PDF rendering, and store\nrate-limit/TTL covered by behavioral tests.\n\nNOTE: C1 also requires provisioning Redis and setting REDIS_URL in Railway — an\ninfrastructure step the code now supports and surfaces but cannot perform itself.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H6KZ3kfjGQK7SjWKUL2NhM\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQuHnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYmsQAEjcITcQQsWdmCFO0yzwGlPM\nMxoz2O67cTzz1isaMcl9sq+QXNDfONrxP+v0DftImsmXviieKjivHoe8qDQ/ZQKx\nJERguXh4ZIqb3a7ct097SY2HZV4vN1Jx5+HjhHyUPCR3G7MZTne8zOHLCf4UClML\ngm8k0c0F6oNrAXGm5xr1VcsRG6K0lCSm2Pwkzx/kEd8cbxTuyEn+CYGe7HmPouFC\nOScRwxwy2+cIz2b5pMpBq8bm9N1Q+RSBJLmrDB+xynFVwh98nhqhQ/xXWIpizY2f\ndPWo752z8Jrg+prOQ3D515KHbAezvFDtwDcKR6Bi7bu7gCIeTJ7yO6fJcbZ95nXr\nyHPFQBnONv90VmZwrhyJ7Epl/3e6gqS+vlRo5LuXt1IdH0+gMwF5O+oxukrpakFm\n0oKn1aTl097xFJnyD7Rc0U+cAbso58EAEL9KwOY5xLmzADqT0Wh+G0lSLGYfJFE6\nGl7bWqorPK55UPBaqGicAT+JfJZ3iow1EM7YmiWCjfxiDBTCeNoHl6ZdaoCRUPaf\nHx/sWm3cmD15ZRQfMzQ5lpfvaxc6clz3U5ES3FMQOXIGLUhOTlEks2vIoNmx4/mQ\nQ+ZaJrADBkUuzZQQy7PjWtf+cWhyvOF+bAxU/VCOerf5m4mAkZU5l8sdU7zqt9X8\nguji1l7h+zoR9LpNgm0d\n=LpUv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/eb98eae95d928530ec80c3b6fbf094792e71a491","node_id":"C_kwDOQkVc4doAKGViOThlYWU5NWQ5Mjg1MzBlYzgwYzNiNmZiZjA5NDc5MmU3MWE0OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/233c3d0ee5341d93f97c25ac9cc16f68e9ee789a","sha":"233c3d0ee5341d93f97c25ac9cc16f68e9ee789a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/233c3d0ee5341d93f97c25ac9cc16f68e9ee789a"}],"sha":"eb98eae95d928530ec80c3b6fbf094792e71a491","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/eb98eae95d928530ec80c3b6fbf094792e71a491"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nzeckets","id":80357080,"login":"nzeckets","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzU3MDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/233c3d0ee5341d93f97c25ac9cc16f68e9ee789a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T20:38:53Z","email":"80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nick Zeckets"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T20:38:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Classify Anthropic errors; fix recurring Anysite 412 and HubSpot 400 (#27)\n\nThree independent reliability fixes the surrogate crash surfaced:\n\n1. Anthropic error handling (analyze.js): the catch block labeled every\n   failure \"We are experiencing high demand,\" so a hard 400 (invalid\n   request body) looked like a traffic spike. Classify on status: 429/\n   529/5xx and overloaded_error are transient and keep the capacity\n   message; non-retryable 4xx now gets an honest error and is logged at\n   error level with the response body so it is visible as a bug.\n\n2. Anysite sn_search 412 (anysite.js): the Sales-Navigator decision-maker\n   search passed current_companies as a bare string and ran even with only\n   a company name, so it 412''d on essentially every run and fell through to\n   the employee listing. Pass current_companies as an array of URNs (the\n   shape the sibling jobs endpoint documents), only attempt it when a real\n   company URN exists, and stop logging the expected fallback as an error.\n\n3. HubSpot create 400 (analyze.js + hubspot.js): createContact sent a\n   linkedin_url property that does not exist on the portal, so every\n   new-contact create 400''d. That left contactId null and silently skipped\n   pushAnalysisToContact, so brand-new leads never had their report attached\n   to the contact. Drop the invalid property from create and store the\n   LinkedIn URL via a new gtmos_linkedin_url property in pushAnalysisToContact\n   (which runs well after ensureProperties, avoiding a cold-start race).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H6KZ3kfjGQK7SjWKUL2NhM\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b32b78db5fe74069dd7cb227992ee54cbe780405","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/b32b78db5fe74069dd7cb227992ee54cbe780405"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/233c3d0ee5341d93f97c25ac9cc16f68e9ee789a","verification":{"payload":"tree b32b78db5fe74069dd7cb227992ee54cbe780405\nparent 850d1896da63ec9124bf1f6db83ea09a609af63f\nauthor Nick Zeckets <80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com> 1782765533 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782765533 -0400\n\nClassify Anthropic errors; fix recurring Anysite 412 and HubSpot 400 (#27)\n\nThree independent reliability fixes the surrogate crash surfaced:\n\n1. Anthropic error handling (analyze.js): the catch block labeled every\n   failure \"We are experiencing high demand,\" so a hard 400 (invalid\n   request body) looked like a traffic spike. Classify on status: 429/\n   529/5xx and overloaded_error are transient and keep the capacity\n   message; non-retryable 4xx now gets an honest error and is logged at\n   error level with the response body so it is visible as a bug.\n\n2. Anysite sn_search 412 (anysite.js): the Sales-Navigator decision-maker\n   search passed current_companies as a bare string and ran even with only\n   a company name, so it 412''d on essentially every run and fell through to\n   the employee listing. Pass current_companies as an array of URNs (the\n   shape the sibling jobs endpoint documents), only attempt it when a real\n   company URN exists, and stop logging the expected fallback as an error.\n\n3. HubSpot create 400 (analyze.js + hubspot.js): createContact sent a\n   linkedin_url property that does not exist on the portal, so every\n   new-contact create 400''d. That left contactId null and silently skipped\n   pushAnalysisToContact, so brand-new leads never had their report attached\n   to the contact. Drop the invalid property from create and store the\n   LinkedIn URL via a new gtmos_linkedin_url property in pushAnalysisToContact\n   (which runs well after ensureProperties, avoiding a cold-start race).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H6KZ3kfjGQK7SjWKUL2NhM\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQtfdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwDsQAJTo0nXnVMf5Si/wtkmo+qwc\nxDEe7IBO8bP4d6j0tcCWxZzBQA2kLCJ8eMjpMl8oEK/qPpeIY7rmSlPw6ltrD3iL\n8sVYcSykRn53o+2F3K/jwu6BhZ6fQKM/DRhpqCzVTZ0gQGLJ6l4l8CwExQ4DaPEj\n4rIwU/OzDYCwlMxg6HOADq1nqjnf/aCPS0v+4IB6Q+krBh5XIVnqgKVVCUv8//X+\nilXPYACBhmr/XGzFhZQiMWk2nN1OWsCOQCfBnmImWibi+wDmPcG4IZrniVr7+nnC\nZBGUxh3qiu1z875uTNPGUKWD8kzkrY5avHJszTf4gTUgMYlUgV9e7cTwJTNm6Dp2\nD6lCXo0H4TgYURleWNuUCesiiYNT2hmRfeHTSHe7rLeMYTDqtxTRq0BZcfbiLykm\nWI+qXPkxUNmqo3YLTwha+LBqhR/bcKPMPjVq4TmhfLUzbC4tOsu64kWe/NK05Ejj\n6ER/H8y+gmN66vTHvTjqhCVAXqLbQaP9wbiACojeim283Et6C7xYjSgnvo3UgBei\ncbT90nP1YyDe6ZLkxsHDYU9vMxDc6nMja/O9M6gLu7CN1GKkLtniAJQCoXEnfnct\nKo6p5lLp+mEEiZW/kiDE/Z3tWM3S9PHnPuwHVQZzlel+a7O7eBJSLjQ0+uwKL06b\nV6IUgsloA6GFPMbw/JEz\n=mNhB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T20:38:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/233c3d0ee5341d93f97c25ac9cc16f68e9ee789a","node_id":"C_kwDOQkVc4doAKDIzM2MzZDBlZTUzNDFkOTNmOTdjMjVhYzljYzE2ZjY4ZTllZTc4OWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/850d1896da63ec9124bf1f6db83ea09a609af63f","sha":"850d1896da63ec9124bf1f6db83ea09a609af63f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/850d1896da63ec9124bf1f6db83ea09a609af63f"}],"sha":"233c3d0ee5341d93f97c25ac9cc16f68e9ee789a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/233c3d0ee5341d93f97c25ac9cc16f68e9ee789a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nzeckets","id":80357080,"login":"nzeckets","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzU3MDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/850d1896da63ec9124bf1f6db83ea09a609af63f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T20:33:37Z","email":"80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nick Zeckets"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T20:33:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix crash: strip unpaired UTF-16 surrogates before Anthropic calls (#26)\n\nLinkedIn posts and decision-maker bios are full of emoji and other\nastral-plane characters. The prompt builder truncates that text with\nslice(), which counts UTF-16 code units, so a cut can land between a\nhigh and low surrogate and leave an orphan. JSON.stringify emits the\nlone surrogate as an invalid \\uD8xx escape, so the Anthropic API\nrejects the whole request body:\n\n  400 invalid_request_error: The request body is not valid JSON:\n  no low surrogate in string\n\nEvery retry hit the same bad byte and never recovered, so the run\nsurfaced the generic \"We are experiencing high demand\" error to the\nuser (e.g. the YPulse analysis that repeated this 400 three times).\n\nAdd stripLoneSurrogates() and apply it to all text sent to Anthropic\nin both the analysis and chat paths, guaranteeing the request body\nalways serializes to valid JSON regardless of the upstream source.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H6KZ3kfjGQK7SjWKUL2NhM\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"750502939f530258b28ea9f34403bcf15594f6d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/750502939f530258b28ea9f34403bcf15594f6d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/850d1896da63ec9124bf1f6db83ea09a609af63f","verification":{"payload":"tree 750502939f530258b28ea9f34403bcf15594f6d2\nparent 9989104d7aafdb4065c5d1efb5f219c95a527bc5\nauthor Nick Zeckets <80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com> 1782765217 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782765217 -0400\n\nFix crash: strip unpaired UTF-16 surrogates before Anthropic calls (#26)\n\nLinkedIn posts and decision-maker bios are full of emoji and other\nastral-plane characters. The prompt builder truncates that text with\nslice(), which counts UTF-16 code units, so a cut can land between a\nhigh and low surrogate and leave an orphan. JSON.stringify emits the\nlone surrogate as an invalid \\uD8xx escape, so the Anthropic API\nrejects the whole request body:\n\n  400 invalid_request_error: The request body is not valid JSON:\n  no low surrogate in string\n\nEvery retry hit the same bad byte and never recovered, so the run\nsurfaced the generic \"We are experiencing high demand\" error to the\nuser (e.g. the YPulse analysis that repeated this 400 three times).\n\nAdd stripLoneSurrogates() and apply it to all text sent to Anthropic\nin both the analysis and chat paths, guaranteeing the request body\nalways serializes to valid JSON regardless of the upstream source.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H6KZ3kfjGQK7SjWKUL2NhM\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQtahCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2CcQAIRR6yvlA7O/luA0wdJt07W1\nr5VbN/Zg5Sc78frPZiQafQMKWR4efexpyLtWan3AJQEE8ZIM6cBCY1t5bCT0X3Ry\nfjVI3GQHa3nneNQ/yoy279s7fqoVJRXuQqhQ+7RmzS6a7rT7ZUqc9F7H1hFxoRDU\n07k9tQoklBoDJiw6VuVZXvrjTlMmfMGxMzT/ggIFbCG79hh3RyKPuYbHhm3eb36P\nAGKBaL2qpfrpFMv8Z6fjOZXCzjwOw5tjtzvYH8nh1eIG55aeT2etcNpFg264Eezs\nM70n9y15+jjpNwqiUqj9yJYihV+k06oRQA1XUEBg+AtnkPQiRjypbqAkJPfkJG+1\nXYWECVXMtwXPg2Ab+7aiEk97B8qcIkwulP4NtaPidAD/95jZXAKlRnZa1aAPdNnH\nLkCh4jkbUXJvIoyiOKWGpMtkRz3Vh+EyMoEBchpJ9h5QHbe1tymtSp5iZNLmpYNU\nIMdttO6yR7OG58a3xL6AutG4rzQMZSiShgm3P/0IuOz3VokO9CCBigeKws+GNxsN\npuxZAx6sWkjK5WIf2/ganIEVpU8ANe63gghP/iE3nfq04FLKZ1iqEv4PCt1O7X5i\nUvysGYR7hrCxZnKXBCmEZTTO4T3nmk/voRacC+LJJkhjq8X86lxq2UWReLKSKOUz\nQsEKY/N60LZtywyxuk9X\n=Twgt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T20:33:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/850d1896da63ec9124bf1f6db83ea09a609af63f","node_id":"C_kwDOQkVc4doAKDg1MGQxODk2ZGE2M2VjOTEyNGJmMWY2ZGI4M2VhMDlhNjA5YWY2M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/9989104d7aafdb4065c5d1efb5f219c95a527bc5","sha":"9989104d7aafdb4065c5d1efb5f219c95a527bc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/9989104d7aafdb4065c5d1efb5f219c95a527bc5"}],"sha":"850d1896da63ec9124bf1f6db83ea09a609af63f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/850d1896da63ec9124bf1f6db83ea09a609af63f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nzeckets","id":80357080,"login":"nzeckets","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzU3MDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/9989104d7aafdb4065c5d1efb5f219c95a527bc5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-18T01:59:47Z","email":"80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nick Zeckets"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-18T01:59:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Gate report payload behind the unlock flow (#25)\n\nGET /api/analysis/:id returned the full report as JSON with no email,\nwhich let anyone holding a share link skip the email capture. Nothing in\nthe app calls it anymore (the page uses the gated /unlock POST). Refuse\nthe bare GET (403) without looking the id up, so report content is only\nreachable through the email gate and existence is never revealed.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QtpcTWqFzR3BSCDa6CFLRg\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e3d00a14b2b61ac4149f3302bddc43f8b0303a18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/e3d00a14b2b61ac4149f3302bddc43f8b0303a18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/9989104d7aafdb4065c5d1efb5f219c95a527bc5","verification":{"payload":"tree e3d00a14b2b61ac4149f3302bddc43f8b0303a18\nparent 31654612e64fd1ccb9b15a224367401e0413745c\nauthor Nick Zeckets <80357080+nzeckets@users.noreply.github.com> 1781747987 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781747987 -0400\n\nGate report payload behind the unlock flow (#25)\n\nGE