users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/857f13c2bd392af0140789f1305704fa78eb10d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T16:34:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T16:34:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix Anysite queries to the real API + detect HubSpot from site source\n\nThe logs showed the old queries were wrong: /api/ai_based/* 404''d (gone) and the\n/api/linkedin/* calls had wrong params. Person-by-email 404''d, so no profile URN\nwas obtained and posts were never fetched (the \"nothing used\" issue).\n\nRewired to the authoritative spec (docs.anysite.io/llms-linkedin.json):\n- Person:  POST /api/linkedin/email/user { email } -> profile incl. fsd_profile URN\n- Posts:   POST /api/linkedin/user/posts { urn, count }  (URN, not a URL slug)\n- Company: POST /api/linkedin/company { company } -> name, logo_url, urn\n- Jobs:    POST /api/linkedin/search/jobs { company: <company URN>, count }\n- Chain: email -> profile URN -> posts; company id -> profile -> URN -> jobs.\n\nHubSpot tiering: the BuiltWith endpoint doesn''t exist. Detect HubSpot directly\nfrom the scraped page source (hs-scripts, hsforms, hubapi, etc.) - instant and\ndeterministic. Removed checkBuiltWith.\n\nAdded [gtmos] logging at each step (profile URN present, posts/jobs counts,\ncompany/logo found, hubspot) so the live pipeline is verifiable from Railway logs.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015xZN5Dikjgt4e47EwDJ2P8","tree":{"sha":"1e770478157da3f79ba70435eb732afb978cd0cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/1e770478157da3f79ba70435eb732afb978cd0cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/857f13c2bd392af0140789f1305704fa78eb10d7","verification":{"payload":"tree 1e770478157da3f79ba70435eb732afb978cd0cf\nparent 4ea3d439edccb2ae3af207e29c51b8bcd594b788\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781454872 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781454872 +0000\n\nFix Anysite queries to the real API + detect HubSpot from site source\n\nThe logs showed the old queries were wrong: /api/ai_based/* 404''d (gone) and the\n/api/linkedin/* calls had wrong params. Person-by-email 404''d, so no profile URN\nwas obtained and posts were never fetched (the \"nothing used\" issue).\n\nRewired to the authoritative spec (docs.anysite.io/llms-linkedin.json):\n- Person:  POST /api/linkedin/email/user { email } -> profile incl. fsd_profile URN\n- Posts:   POST /api/linkedin/user/posts { urn, count }  (URN, not a URL slug)\n- Company: POST /api/linkedin/company { company } -> name, logo_url, urn\n- Jobs:    POST /api/linkedin/search/jobs { company: <company URN>, count }\n- Chain: email -> profile URN -> posts; company id -> profile -> URN -> jobs.\n\nHubSpot tiering: the BuiltWith endpoint doesn''t exist. Detect HubSpot directly\nfrom the scraped page source (hs-scripts, hsforms, hubapi, etc.) - instant and\ndeterministic. Removed checkBuiltWith.\n\nAdded [gtmos] logging at each step (profile URN present, posts/jobs counts,\ncompany/logo found, hubspot) so the live pipeline is verifiable from Railway logs.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015xZN5Dikjgt4e47EwDJ2P8\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJTIZQBR\nARSjFkXeHt6rRDXnRUoB25a38Eg4saIsrn5fI1UfxqxJ0JSFwxyRGprH0qFn9n/SGUnmulDDh6AT\nKAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-14T16:34:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/857f13c2bd392af0140789f1305704fa78eb10d7","node_id":"C_kwDOQkVc4doAKDg1N2YxM2MyYmQzOTJhZjAxNDA3ODlmMTMwNTcwNGZhNzhlYjEwZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commit/4ea3d439edccb2ae3af207e29c51b8bcd594b788","sha":"4ea3d439edccb2ae3af207e29c51b8bcd594b788","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/4ea3d439edccb2ae3af207e29c51b8bcd594b788"}],"sha":"857f13c2bd392af0140789f1305704fa78eb10d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/857f13c2bd392af0140789f1305704fa78eb10d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80357080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzeckets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.c