ignals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/5ca451df0985a90ee2ebc11f183dcd6edaf049af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/commits/eb78215a93721b8ef05de1f859600a1a48ee37b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T15:53:45Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T15:53:45Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Reframe app as market-facing, kill AI-slop voice, connect the flywheel\n\n- Voice: ban AI-slop constructions (the \"not A, but B\" hook, \"X is dead\",\n  \"Here''s the thing\", etc.); require concrete, specific, operator-voice hooks.\n- Section 3 app is now market-facing: an app the company would deploy to its\n  OWN ICP prospects (like GTM OS), seeded by the alpha signal and valuable to\n  their buyer, not a tool that scores the visitor as a lead. Added an on-page\n  eyebrow making that explicit.\n- Section 4 outbound now gives the interactive app and long-form insight as the\n  value, tying outbound, content, and the app into one motion.\n- Section 5 LinkedIn plan modeled on a proven operator post (story + specifics +\n  comment-to-get-it CTA) and routes to the app as the lead magnet.\n- Made the flywheel explicit across the report: signal -> app + content ->\n  social -> leads.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015xZN5Dikjgt4e47EwDJ2P8","tree":{"sha":"7f88c9ed3dacba8c966383aeddce4724877413b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/trees/7f88c9ed3dacba8c966383aeddce4724877413b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Smoke-Signals-AI/gtm-os-analysis/git/commits/eb78215a93721b8ef05de1f859600a1a48ee37b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f88c9ed3dacba8c966383aeddce4724877413b7\nparent c81e8f3ee6df91adb7b03b9f3609a01b337a0d9e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781452425 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781452425 +0000\n\nReframe app as market-facing, kill AI-slop voice, connect the flywheel\n\n- Voice: ban AI-slop constructions (the \"not A, but B\" hook, \"X is dead\",\n  \"Here''s the thing\", etc.); require concrete, specific, operator-voice hooks.\n- Section 3 app is now market-facing: an app the company would deploy to its\n  OWN ICP prospects (like GTM OS), seeded by the alpha signal and valuable to\n  their buyer, not a tool that scores the visitor as a lead. Added an on-page\n  eyebrow making that explicit.\n- Section 4 outbound now gives the interactive app and long-form insight as the\n  value, tying outbound, content, and the app into one motion.\n- Section 5 LinkedIn plan modeled on a proven operator post (story + specifics +\n  comment-to-get-it CTA) and routes to the app as the lead magnet.\n- Made the flywheel explicit across the report: signal -> app + content ->\n  social -> leads.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015xZN5Dikjgt4e47EwDJ2P8\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE